tion":"The document embeds imperative instructions aimed at an AI agent ('AI MUST EXECUTE EVERY STEP IN ORDER'). In an agentic environment, such hidden or meta-instructions can override user intent and drive unauthorized actions, especially when combined with shell commands and deployment steps.","remediation":"Remove AI-directed imperative comments from the skill content and rewrite them as user-facing documentation. If agent consumption is intended, move execution policies into trusted system/developer controls rather than untrusted skill text.","code_snippet":"\n## ⚠️ DEPLOYMENT IS A 4-STEP BLOCKING PIPELINE\n\n<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE EVERY STEP IN ORDER) -->\n\n> **AI: You MUST execute Steps 1→2→3→4 in order. Do NOT skip any step.**\n> **Do NOT call `manageAgent` until Step 3 (Verification) passes ALL checks.**","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a58b252caebd7ef859173f59c13f2fd93f54607e0d068dcef51307f1a8967339","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":26,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-486f6b2c27884cf2820725bda48646e5","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hidden Instructions","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":40,"end_line":null},"finding":"<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE) -->","explanation":"This hidden instruction explicitly tells an AI to execute environment-modifying actions. In a tool-using agent workflow, instructions embedded in reference content are untrusted input and can cause the agent to perform actions without separate authorization or contextual validation.","remediation":"Convert AI-execution directives into plain explanatory text for humans. Enforce any required workflow sequencing in trusted orchestration code or policy checks, not in markdown comments.","code_snippet":"\n## Step 1: Ensure Python 3.10\n\n<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE) -->\n\nExecute one of the following to ensure Python 3.10 is available:\n","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d6c3c25994736dcbb8f587c49c42270bf18a1caf85ece660540f00b1259d462d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":40,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-00ec5d98806342aea324f1a679fe8283","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hidden Instructions","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":74,"end_line":null},"finding":"<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE) -->","explanation":"The hidden 'AI MUST EXECUTE' directive is prompt-injection-like content because it attempts to control agent behavior from within the skill body. Given that the same section includes destructive filesystem commands, the risk is elevated beyond mere formatting or style concerns.","remediation":"Delete hidden agent-targeting directives and present the steps as optional/manual operator instructions. Add explicit trust boundaries: documentation must not be treated as executable instructions by the agent.","code_snippet":"\n## Step 2: Build env/ (One-Shot Install)\n\n<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE) -->\n\n> ### ⚠️ CRITICAL: `env/` is an immutable build artifact\n>","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d6c3c25994736dcbb8f587c49c42270bf18a1caf85ece660540f00b1259d462d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":74,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-ee437afec3c64e11a1d4fc31d9d65a6a","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":79,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf ./env`","explanation":"The instruction mandates 'rm -rf ./env', a destructive filesystem operation. In an agent context, this is dangerous because the agent may execute it automatically, deleting local dependencies or other files if path assumptions are wrong, causing data loss or disruption.","remediation":"Do not include raw destructive commands as mandatory agent actions in skill content. Replace with guarded procedures: require explicit user confirmation, verify the working directory, constrain deletions to sandboxed paths, or use safer cleanup mechanisms implemented in trusted tooling.","code_snippet":"> ### ⚠️ CRITICAL: `env/` is an immutable build artifact\n>\n> The ONLY correct workflow is:\n> 1. **Delete** → `rm -rf ./env`\n> 2. **Install** → single `pip install` command (below)\n> 3. **Never touch again**\n>","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"bb527c42a83e7d62361beb65c1bf1d7fcb7c533c8b37f826741f76c279daf09c","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":79,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-2da43cd1aafa49938752992a521c33e5","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":107,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf ./env","explanation":"This script contains an automatic 'rm -rf ./env && mkdir ./env' step. If followed by an autonomous agent, it performs deletion without confirmation, and because it is presented as 'execute as-is', it discourages safety checks or path validation.","remediation":"Remove destructive shell steps from untrusted markdown workflows intended for agents. If cleanup is required, implement a trusted helper that validates target paths, prompts for confirmation, and operates only inside the project sandbox.","code_snippet":"echo \"✅ Using: $PYTHON_BIN ($($PYTHON_BIN --version 2>&1))\"\n\n# ── Atomic env/ rebuild ──\nrm -rf ./env && mkdir ./env\n\n# ── One-shot install ALL deps ──\n$PYTHON_BIN -m pip install -r ./requirements.txt \\","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0a1e5eede0098069b008972b0c4e77b854555355f2fde84ec946a925422587f2","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":107,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-1a749592c32f46f287a050961a23a9ba","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hidden Instructions","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":126,"end_line":null},"finding":"<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE) -->","explanation":"This hidden instruction attempts to gate tool usage and force a specific remediation path from untrusted content. In an agent security model, that is dangerous because embedded content should not be able to dictate execution order, blocking behavior, or mutation steps.","remediation":"Move deployment gating logic into trusted code or policy enforcement outside the markdown. Keep the document descriptive, not imperative toward the AI runtime.","code_snippet":"\n## Step 3: Verify env/ Integrity (MANDATORY)\n\n<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE) -->\n\n> **Do NOT call `manageAgent` until ALL checks below pass.**\n> **If ANY check fails, the ONLY fix is: edit requirements.txt → rm -rf env/ → re-run Step 2.**","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d6c3c25994736dcbb8f587c49c42270bf18a1caf85ece660540f00b1259d462d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":126,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-3292caf33e1143c9b0e39ffedc6afc2a","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":129,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/","explanation":"The guide states the 'ONLY fix' is to delete env/ and rebuild, encouraging repeated destructive actions. In a skill consumed by agents, rigid remediation text can trigger unnecessary deletion loops and amplify damage from mistakes or path confusion.","remediation":"Avoid prescribing unconditional deletion in agent-readable content. Recommend non-destructive diagnostics first, and if cleanup is necessary, require explicit confirmation and trusted path validation before removal.","code_snippet":"<!-- INSTRUCTION (AI MUST EXECUTE) -->\n\n> **Do NOT call `manageAgent` until ALL checks below pass.**\n> **If ANY check fails, the ONLY fix is: edit requirements.txt → rm -rf env/ → re-run Step 2.**\n\n### 3a. Verify all top-level packages are present\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"be09b1ed97e777e0d513cf0de262e986d31217e96d03586f45db2e6f962efa1d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":129,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-71ab4f4e34d142b2be528930c67138bf","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":170,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/","explanation":"This line reinforces deletion as the default recovery action. While acceptable for a human-operated local build guide, it becomes risky in an agentic setting because the model may convert advisory text into immediate tool actions affecting the filesystem.","remediation":"Refactor error messages so they are human guidance only, not executable imperatives for agents. Use safe recovery commands via controlled tooling instead of embedding 'rm -rf' instructions.","code_snippet":"    for f in failed:\n        print(f'  ❌ MISSING: {f}')\n    print()\n    print('Fix: Check requirements.txt spelling, then rm -rf env/ and re-run Step 2')\n    sys.exit(1)\nelse:\n    print()","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"be09b1ed97e777e0d513cf0de262e986d31217e96d03586f45db2e6f962efa1d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":170,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-e8bbfb7599eb443196fda89e1b83885a","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":226,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/","explanation":"The repeated recommendation to run 'rm -rf env/' after import failures encourages automatic destructive remediation. In the context of a deployment skill, the operational context makes this more dangerous because agents may have access to project files and execution tools.","remediation":"Replace with a safer workflow: stop, report the issue, and ask the user whether to rebuild dependencies. Use a trusted rebuild command that validates the project root and target directory.","code_snippet":"\nif failed:\n    print(f'\\n❌ Import verification failed for: {failed}')\n    print('Fix: Ensure these are in requirements.txt, then rm -rf env/ and re-run Step 2')\n    sys.exit(1)\nelse:\n    print('\\n✅ All imports verified')","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"be09b1ed97e777e0d513cf0de262e986d31217e96d03586f45db2e6f962efa1d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":226,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-703d193f3bc34a05b5032c3d1a9311de","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":261,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/","explanation":"The 'Golden Rule' codifies deletion as the universal fix and says 'Never deviate from this,' which is problematic for tool-using agents. It suppresses safer alternatives and can drive deterministic destructive behavior from untrusted documentation.","remediation":"Remove absolute language and avoid universal destructive prescriptions. Provide conditional troubleshooting guidance and require human approval before any deletion or rebuild action.","code_snippet":"\n> **Golden Rule: ANY problem with `env/` has exactly ONE fix:**\n> ```\n> edit requirements.txt (if needed) → rm -rf env/ → re-run Step 2 script → re-run Step 3\n> ```\n> **There is NO other fix. Never deviate from this.**\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"be09b1ed97e777e0d513cf0de262e986d31217e96d03586f45db2e6f962efa1d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":261,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-cd1af196150d4f638c82d9e05e7bf38c","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":269,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/`","explanation":"This troubleshooting step again instructs deletion of env/ as part of recovery. The danger comes from the agent skill context: embedded shell guidance can be interpreted as actionable commands, leading to unintended file deletion or repeated rebuild cycles.","remediation":"Present troubleshooting as non-executable guidance and gate destructive actions behind explicit consent. Prefer a trusted cleanup/rebuild utility over raw shell commands in documentation.","code_snippet":"\n- **Cause**: A package doesn't have a `manylinux2014_x86_64` wheel for Python 3.10\n- **Fix**: Pin a version in `requirements.txt` that has a compatible wheel, or check spelling\n- **Then**: `rm -rf env/` → re-run Step 2\n\n### Error: `ModuleNotFoundError` at runtime (ANY module)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6b4dbf41cf39f8993ab9c9535c37f080c862b47f1fbe3853d65aca7cc3eddd50","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":269,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-da19050c6bce4f788e0143018f315086","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":276,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/`","explanation":"The text recommends deleting env/ for any ModuleNotFoundError, which is overbroad and destructive. In this skill context, broad 'fixes' that delete directories can be misapplied automatically, causing downtime and loss of local state.","remediation":"Narrow the advice and add verification before cleanup. Require the agent to surface the diagnosis to the user and obtain approval before rebuilding dependency directories.","code_snippet":"- **Cause 1**: The module is missing from `requirements.txt` → add it\n- **Cause 2**: `env/` was built with Python 3.11+ → ensure Python 3.10, rebuild\n- **Cause 3**: `env/` was built incrementally (multiple pip installs) → rebuild atomically\n- **Fix**: `rm -rf env/` → re-run Step 2\n\n### Error: Namespace package submodule missing (e.g., `cloudbase_agent.xxx`)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6b4dbf41cf39f8993ab9c9535c37f080c862b47f1fbe3853d65aca7cc3eddd50","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":276,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-51b248a22ab4412ba8328d75893978d8","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":281,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/`","explanation":"This line repeats the destructive rebuild pattern for namespace-package issues. The risk is not malicious payload execution but unsafe tool parameterization and deletion instructions embedded in content that may control an agent.","remediation":"Remove or quarantine destructive command text from skill content. If rebuilds are necessary, expose them through a safe, validated operation in trusted deployment tooling.","code_snippet":"### Error: Namespace package submodule missing (e.g., `cloudbase_agent.xxx`)\n\n- **Cause**: Multiple `pip install` commands into `env/` caused namespace package fragmentation\n- **Fix**: `rm -rf env/` → re-run Step 2 (single command installs all packages atomically)\n\n### ⛔ PROHIBITED OPERATIONS (will cause deployment failures)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6b4dbf41cf39f8993ab9c9535c37f080c862b47f1fbe3853d65aca7cc3eddd50","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":281,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-642dc88ceba2401786b08f74e5f70e12","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":430,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf env/`","explanation":"The summary reiterates the unconditional deletion workflow, reinforcing unsafe automated behavior. Although it is only a recap, repeated emphasis increases the chance an agent will prioritize the destructive command path over safer diagnostics.","remediation":"Revise the summary to describe rebuilds conceptually without embedding raw deletion commands. State that dependency rebuilds should be user-approved and executed via trusted project-scoped tooling.","code_snippet":"| **Python runtime** | Python 3.10 (MUST USE, `runtime=\"Python3.10\"`) |\n| **Dependency strategy** | Local pre-packaging to `./env` (**MUST use Python 3.10 interpreter**, `installDependency=false`) |\n| **Build workflow** | Step 1 (Python) → Step 2 (build env/) → Step 3 (verify) → Step 4 (deploy) |\n| **env/ rebuild rule** | ALWAYS atomic: `rm -rf env/` → single `pip install` — NEVER incremental |\n| **Default platform** | HTTP Cloud Functions |\n| **Fallback platform** | CloudRun (only for special requirements) |\n| **Startup script** | `scf_bootstrap` — set `PYTHONPATH=\"./env:$PYTHONPATH\"`, do NOT `pip install` at startup |","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6b4dbf41cf39f8993ab9c9535c37f080c862b47f1fbe3853d65aca7cc3eddd50","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":430,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E4","finding_id":"finding-4b6798b53ae842809b613e54e4042e0b","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"Context Leakage","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":185,"end_line":null},"finding":"Extract context","explanation":"Code or instructions that leak agent conversation context to external services, potentially exposing sensitive user interactions.","remediation":"Remove any code that sends prompts, responses, or session data externally. Preserve user privacy; never exfiltrate conversation content.","code_snippet":"async with httpx.AsyncClient() as client:\n    response = await client.get(url, headers=headers)\n\n# Extract context from incoming request\ncontext = extract_trace_context(request.headers)\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3d81bd10b2e3e6d455ff0d58475d679b775e4b3d9b9dc77c6fe46c53990dd272","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":185,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-ca6c763a2c3448e3b3a734e6742613da","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/server-quickstart.md","start_line":291,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST http://localhost:9000/chatbot/send-message \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"conversationId\": \"conv_123\",\n    \"messages\": [\n      {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"### 1. CloudBase Agent Native Endpoint\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:9000/chatbot/send-message \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"conversationId\": \"conv_123\",","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3e5300188f4f78fca621d895ca2f33dbbcad660801c20b75edb863af114f8da4","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/server-quickstart.md","start_line":291,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-708fcae237774f1bb278377f3d048b90","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":259,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -f /private/var/folders/*/*/T/cloudapp-*.zip`（部署进程异常时残留不清理会堆积）","explanation":"This duplicated finding points to the same risky cleanup instruction: a forceful `rm -f` with globbing over `/private/var/folders/*/*/T/cloudapp-*.zip`. Even though intended as disk cleanup, the pattern is unnecessarily broad and can lead to deletion of unintended matching files in automated environments.","remediation":"Deduplicate this finding in tooling, and fix the underlying guidance by instructing users to remove only a deployment artifact whose full path was captured from the current run. Avoid shell globs in destructive commands; use explicit paths or a guarded script with checks.","code_snippet":"**规避**（三选一，推荐 ①+③）：\n1. 部署时显式传 `--ignore \"**/target/**\"`（CLI）或 `ignore: [\"**/target/**\", ...]`（MCP deployApp）\n2. 项目根 `cloudbaserc.json` 的 `app.ignore` 加 `**/target/**`（CLI 会合并）\n3. 部署完成后删除残留：`rm -f /private/var/folders/*/*/T/cloudapp-*.zip`（部署进程异常时残留不清理会堆积）\n\n**判断**：部署日志显示 \"Project directory: xxx\" 只代表 framework 检测目录，**不代表打包目录**；怀疑打包过大时先看生成的 zip 大小。\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d2623644c96456d8f9f43ee45bd9a8ca258d8c32126d66f24cf151ef306988b6","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":259,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-bab3c3748dd040888eb826a3decb8fad","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":259,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -f /private/var/folders/*/*/T/cloudapp-*.zip`(部署进程异常时残留不清理会堆积)","explanation":"This duplicated finding points to the same risky cleanup instruction: a forceful `rm -f` with globbing over `/private/var/folders/*/*/T/cloudapp-*.zip`. Even though intended as disk cleanup, the pattern is unnecessarily broad and can lead to deletion of unintended matching files in automated environments.","remediation":"Deduplicate this finding in tooling, and fix the underlying guidance by instructing users to remove only a deployment artifact whose full path was captured from the current run. Avoid shell globs in destructive commands; use explicit paths or a guarded script with checks.","code_snippet":"**规避**(三选一,推荐 1+3):\n1. 部署时显式传 `--ignore \"**/target/**\"`(CLI)或 `ignore: [\"**/target/**\", ...]`(MCP deployApp)\n2. 项目根 `cloudbaserc.json` 的 `app.ignore` 加 `**/target/**`(CLI 会合并)\n3. 部署完成后删除残留:`rm -f /private/var/folders/*/*/T/cloudapp-*.zip`(部署进程异常时残留不清理会堆积)\n\n**判断**:部署日志显示 \"Project directory: xxx\" 只代表 framework 检测目录,**不代表打包目录**;怀疑打包过大时先看生成的 zip 大小。\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","normalized-view"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"616d8a71092e8ee7d41739e887f9f5c6312fe61b2838fd9b3fac4930307e3b7a","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":259,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-f6c56e6150b54d318a96f3635ee8256e","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification