ety constraints, or install persistent backdoors.","remediation":"Prevent the skill from modifying its own code, SKILL.md, or configuration files. Treat skill files as read-only at runtime.","code_snippet":"| **Project config sync** | `config init / pull / diff / update` | `cloudbaserc.json` ↔ the cloud |\n\nPlus the project / tooling bootstrap commands: `init`, `new`, `pull`, `open`, `validate`,\n`self-update`, `rollback`, and the **`tcb ai` setup wizard**.\n\n## When to Use\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"acc52580b0a6763c2be5b86ab2142cbb1b9fcd880aebd75d357a5c575d309983","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":366,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-f6c56e6150b54d318a96f3635ee8256e","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":389,"end_line":null},"finding":"self-update","explanation":"Skill modifies its own code, configuration, or behavior at runtime. Self-modification enables an agent to escalate privileges, disable safety constraints, or install persistent backdoors.","remediation":"Prevent the skill from modifying its own code, SKILL.md, or configuration files. Treat skill files as read-only at runtime.","code_snippet":"| **Project config sync** | `config init / pull / diff / update` | `cloudbaserc.json` ↔ the cloud |\n\nPlus the project / tooling bootstrap commands: `init`, `new`, `pull`, `open`, `validate`,\n`self-update`, `rollback`, and the **`tcb ai` setup wizard**.\n\n## When to Use\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"acc52580b0a6763c2be5b86ab2142cbb1b9fcd880aebd75d357a5c575d309983","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":389,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AR1","finding_id":"finding-b24778e385c04d7ab1c61f37b23d66b0","category":"Anti-Refusal","pattern":"Anti-Refusal Statement","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/functions.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null},"finding":"always answer","explanation":"Skill instructs the agent to never refuse or to always comply. Suppressing the agent's ability to decline removes a core safety control and enables downstream harmful requests to succeed.","remediation":"Remove any instruction telling the agent to never refuse or always comply. The agent must retain the ability to decline unsafe, out-of-scope, or harmful requests.","code_snippet":"> - `tcb fn log <name>` → **`tcb logs search`** (deprecated since v3.0.0; CLS query syntax, see Workflow 3)\n\n> 🚫 **Two separate function command families still register and are NOT `tcb fn`.** They are\n> **not recommended for use** — always answer with `tcb fn`:\n> - **`tcb cloudfunction <deploy|download|run>`** — 云函数服务 (older service API; uses\n>   `-s/--serviceName` + `--source`, not `fn`'s `--path` / `--dir` / `[name]` shape)\n> - **`tcb cloudrunfunction <deploy|download|run>`** — 云函数 2.0 服务 (函数型云托管 lineage)","intent":null,"tags":["Anti-Refusal","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b4404d69f30b43064cedf6b7a3bc0f82006c7ad3e8bc125c4f8dc6a681444289","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/functions.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-c0ef6180563b41b2ac640f3d8f270bed","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/functions.md","start_line":342,"end_line":null},"finding":".env.local\n","explanation":"This documentation instructs users to pull deployed environment variables into a local file, including `.env.local`, which may contain production secrets. That creates a credential exposure path through local disk storage, accidental commits, developer endpoint compromise, shell history, or leakage into logs and tooling; in a CloudBase functions context, env vars commonly hold API keys, DB endpoints, and tokens, so the skill context makes this more sensitive.","remediation":"Avoid recommending bulk export of deployed environment variables unless strictly necessary. If export is required, direct users to a secure temporary path outside the repo, ensure `.env.local`/output files are gitignored, set restrictive file permissions, warn that secrets may be included, and prefer secret-manager or per-secret retrieval workflows over dumping all variables to disk.","code_snippet":"```bash\n# Pull the deployed environment variables of a function into a local file\ntcb fn env pull my-function\ntcb fn env pull my-function --output-file .env.local\n```\n\nThis is the read side. To **write** env vars, edit `envVariables` in `cloudbaserc.json` and push with","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"021f7ffa4122cf8ed26ecae08a0a46ff9aa27fee40f717ab4c3bff5f82c6550e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/functions.md","start_line":342,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-9064418392d24757bb0a7872121e490a","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/functions.md","start_line":372,"end_line":null},"finding":".env.local ","explanation":"Repeating the recommendation to dump function environment variables to `.env.local` reinforces a workflow that materializes deployed secrets onto developer machines. In this operational context, the file may be copied into workspaces, backups, IDE indexes, or accidentally committed, increasing the chance of credential disclosure and downstream compromise of CloudBase-connected services.","remediation":"Remove or soften the example that writes secrets to `.env.local`, or replace it with guidance to inspect values in a secure interface without exporting them. If local export must remain documented, explicitly require `.gitignore` coverage, least-privilege access, secure deletion after use, and a warning that production secrets should not be persisted in project directories.","code_snippet":"tcb config update fn my-function\n# Verify\ntcb fn detail my-function\ntcb fn env pull my-function --output-file .env.local   # or dump them to a file\n```\n\n> 💡 For values you do not want in git, prefer CloudBase-managed configuration over a committed","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"021f7ffa4122cf8ed26ecae08a0a46ff9aa27fee40f717ab4c3bff5f82c6550e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/functions.md","start_line":372,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-0466a007cf7f43c38641497d7530a113","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":300,"end_line":null},"finding":"access token","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"\n- Creating / updating a reusable sandbox **tool** (image, network mode, resources, mounts)\n- Starting, pausing, resuming, stopping sandbox **instances**\n- Fetching an instance's access token\n- Managing sandbox **API keys** for programmatic access\n\n## Do NOT use for","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","contextual-triage","likely-benign-context","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"903a9f18e7222d4c1e39fcf76dec31bef3fd46b6332f4bc5bc823999d287548b","occurrences":[{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_lin