"references/cloudbase-cli/references/sandbox.md","start_line":94,"end_line":null},"finding":"access credential","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"> ⚠️ `instance update --timeout` **restarts the timeout clock** from the moment you set it — it is not\n> \"extend by N\". Minimum 30s, maximum 24h.\n>\n> ⚠️ `instance token` returns a live access credential. Do not print it into logs, commits, or the\n> conversation transcript; hand it to the user, not into a file under version control.\n\n---","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"df484b7063368ca35796b5c12b4e48a26fb517505906763200197ca3751f5b80","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/sandbox.md","start_line":94,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-aeb5f2089c4e4a5fadd430e8f13182df","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":422,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm \"temp/**\"","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"tcb storage rm file.txt -e <envId>                    # Single file\ntcb storage rm file1.txt file2.txt -e <envId>          # Multiple files\ntcb storage rm \"*.log\" -e <envId>                      # Wildcard — current dir only\ntcb storage rm \"temp/**\" -e <