shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"tcb storage rm file1.txt file2.txt -e <envId>          # Multiple files\ntcb storage rm \"*.log\" -e <envId>                      # Wildcard — current dir only\ntcb storage rm \"temp/**\" -e <envId>                    # Recursive wildcard\ntcb storage rm folder/ --dir -e <envId>                # Directory\n```\n\n⚠️ Wildcard patterns **must be quoted** — use `\"*.log\"`, not `*.log`. Unquoted globs expand against your local filesystem, not cloud storage.","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"984358f433ccd493e29e657d4bec73a776ef93620c82fb54ebb4c39b8abf598d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/storage.md","start_line":125,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-d174567d8af0422896bbac55fd06a073","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/storage.md","start_line":144,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm \"**/*.log\"","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"# Only root-level .log files\ntcb storage rm \"*.log\" -e <envId>\n# .log files in ALL directories\ntcb storage rm \"**/*.log\" -e <envId>\n```\n\n---","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"67af5d6c1f8781e367204b342f11e064822cd201619d057e583d9e8635faf491","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/storage.md","start_line":144,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-d174567d8af0422896bbac55fd06a073","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/storage.md","start_line":263,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm \"**/*.log\"","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"# Only root-level .log files\ntcb storage rm \"*.log\" -e <envId>\n# .log files in ALL directories\ntcb storage rm \"**/*.log\" -e <envId>\n```\n\n---","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"67af5d6c1f8781e367204b342f11e064822cd201619d057e583d9e8635faf491","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/storage.md","start_line":263,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-8f457b80563d4fb080b0da276e9986fe","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/storage.md","start_line":327,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm /","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"| | COS storage (default) | PG storage (`pgstore`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Environments | NoSQL / MySQL / default | **PostgreSQL-mode** environments |\n| Object ops | `storage upload / download / rm / list / url / detail / cp / search` | `storage objects upload / download / stat / list / rm / cp / mv / sign` |\n| Buckets | one implicit environment bucket | `storage buckets list` (multi-bucket) |\n| Permission model | `storage rules get / update` (ACL rules) | `storage policies list` — **RLS policies** on `buckets` / `objects` |\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"93f8e16b0a76b46086b464219516b22532f4e81a8d388f0a77555226773a9b79","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/storage.md","start_line":327,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"YR4","finding_id":"finding-77c6751690704cc19a73f783054c080d","category":"YARA Match","pattern":"YARA rule 'agent_skill_prompt_injection_hidden_instructions': Prompt injection or hidden instructions embedded in AI agent skill text [agent_skills]","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":77,"end_line":null},"finding":"model; bypass security","explanation":"YARA rule matched a hack tool or exploit indicator (offensive tools, reconnaissance, privilege escalation, or exploit frameworks).","remediation":"Remove offensive tool references and exploit code. Legitimate agent skills should not contain penetration testing tools, exploit frameworks, or reconnaissance utilities.","code_snippet":"pressions to define permission logic\n- **Dynamic permissions**: Supports dynamic permission judgment based on user identity, time, and data content\n- **Client-only restriction**: Only restricts client user access, does not affect server-side (cloud function) operations\n\n**Configuration Entry:**\nConfigure security rules in the [CloudBase Platform/Database](https://tcb.cloud.tencent.com/dev#/db/doc/model) collection management page.\n\n## Permission Categories\n\nCloudBase provides two types of permissions:\n\n### 1. Simple Permissions (Recommended for Most Cases)\n\nThese are pre-configured permission templates that cover most common scenarios:\n\n- **READONLY**: All users can read, only creator and admin can write\n- **PRIVATE**: Only creator and admin can read/write\n- **ADMINWRITE**: All users can read, only admin can write\n- **ADMINONLY**: Only admin can read/write\n\n### 2. Custom Security Rules (CUSTOM)\n\nUse CUSTOM when you need fine-grained control based on document data, user identity, or com","intent":null,"tags":["YARA Match","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"19c912969f3949c6cabd25f94eced5fcc721e9dd58c7f67e096136f76dea511e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":77,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P1","finding_id":"finding-03976c87fbe847d791eac915dce5e626","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Instruction Override","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":625,"end_line":null},"finding":"bypass security","explanation":"This pattern attempts to override system instructions or ignore safety constraints. Without LLM analysis, manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Remove or rewrite any text that instructs the agent to ignore prompts, override safety rules, or trust unverified content. Ensure skill content cannot be injected to alter agent behavior.","code_snippet":"\n1. Keep frontend collections locked down with `CUSTOM` rules that restrict users to their own data\n2. Build **management console APIs** with **cloud functions** (CloudBase Run or functions)\n3. Cloud functions bypass security rules, so they can read/write all data safely based on backend authentication/authorization\n\n> TL;DR: **Frontend SDK permissions ≠ backend role management.** If a role needs global data access (e.g., admin dashboard), implement it via cloud functions and never expose that data directly through frontend security rules.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f225feace2ebc9a39c615c533be26d4c2d678379bcad9c1dda410cd2aa2ed7e5","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":625,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-54d996e5d5f847b194cb335af98e67d7","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":625,"end_line":null},"finding":"bypass security rule","explanation":"The document explicitly states that cloud functions bypass frontend database security rules and recommends using them for global data access. While architecturally valid, this becomes dangerous if readers implement backend functions without strong server-side authorization, because it can create privileged paths that ignore the collection's client protections and expose all data or allow unrestricted modification.","remediation":"Keep the architectural guidance, but add mandatory safeguards: require explicit backend authentication and role checks on every cloud function, validate input server-side, use least-privilege service accounts, add audit logging, and document that bypassing client rules must never mean bypassing authorization. Include secure code examples showing admin-only enforcement in the function itself.","code_snippet":"\n1. Keep frontend collections locked down with `CUSTOM` rules that restrict users to their own data\n2. Build **management console APIs** with **cloud functions** (CloudBase Run or functions)\n3. Cloud functions bypass security rules, so they can read/write all data safely based on backend authentication/authorization\n\n> TL;DR: **Frontend SDK permissions ≠ backend role management.** If a role needs global data access (e.g., admin dashboard), implement it via cloud functions and never expose that data directly through frontend security rules.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2d1ff620222e634c92bcdf9465af44be04aa4a1ffe0b2415dadd628c2d7ca6e0","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":625,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-eed1cdeab3a74ab69226fe917f111588","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-platform/SKILL.md","start_line":370,"end_line":null},"finding":"update this skill","explanation":"Skill modifies its own code, configuration, or behavior at runtime. Self-modification enables an agent to escalate privileges, disable safety constraints, or install persistent backdoors.","remediation":"Prevent the skill from modifying its own code, SKILL.md, or configuration files. Treat skill files as read-only at runtime.","code_snippet":"\nAfter creating/deploying resources, provide corresponding console links. All console URLs follow the pattern: `https://tcb.cloud.tencent.com/dev?envId=${envId}#/{path}` — replace `${envId}` with the real EnvId resolved via `queryEnv` (resolve aliases first; see Environment and Authentication below), and resource names with actual values.\n\nThe CloudBase console is updated frequently. If a live, logged-in console shows a different hash path from this list, prefer the live console path over stale documentation and then update this skill to match.\n\n### Entry points (one line each)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"41058dad295001d1b21d5c63f2fa99b47ef86748212e67620ca950f6f6b1aaa2","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-platform/SKILL.md","start_line":370,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-b8a5996f9e2e4fd38ac234079f82b005","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":81,"end_line":null},"finding":"access token","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"| Credential | Database role | Where it can live | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Publishable Key | `anon` | Frontend-safe | Still constrained by GRANT/RLS. |\n| User access token | `authenticated` | SDK-managed frontend session | Represents a real logged-in user. |\n| API Key | `service_role` | Backend / trusted tooling only | Bypasses RLS; never expose to browser code. Treat any leak as a serious credential compromise and rotate/revoke it via `manageAppAuth(action=\"deleteApiKey\")` immediately. |\n\n## `auth.users` — the built-in account table","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"903a9f18e7222d4c1e39fcf76dec31bef3fd46b6332f4bc5bc823999d287548b","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":81,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-b8a5996f9e2e4fd38ac234079f82b005","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"access token","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"| Credential | Database role | Where it can live | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Publishable Key | `anon` | Frontend-safe | Still constrained by GRANT/RLS. |\n| User access token | `authenticated` | SDK-managed frontend session | Represents a real logged-in user. |\n| API Key | `service_role` | Backend / trusted tooling only | Bypasses RLS; never expose to browser code. Treat any leak as a serious credential compromise and rotate/revoke it via `manageAppAuth(action=\"deleteApiKey\")` immediately. |\n\n## `auth.users` — the built-in account table","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"903a9f18e7222d4c1e39fcf76dec31bef3fd46b6332f4bc5bc823999d287548b","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-b8a5996f9e2e4fd38ac234079f82b005","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":125,"end_line":null},"finding":"access token","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"| Credential | Database role | Where it can live | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Publishable Key | `anon` | Frontend-safe | Still constrained by GRANT/RLS. |\n| User access token | `authenticated` | SDK-managed frontend session | Represents a real logged-in user. |\n| API Key | `service_role` | Backend / trusted tooling only | Bypasses RLS; never expose to browser code. Treat any leak as a serious credential compromise and rotate/revoke it via `manageAppAuth(action=\"deleteApiKey\")` immediately. |\n\n## `auth.users` — the built-in account table","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"903a9f18e7222d4c1e39fcf76dec31bef3fd46b6332f4bc5bc823999d287548b","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":125,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-b8a5996f9e2e4fd38ac234079f82b005","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":144,"end_line":null},"finding":"access token","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"| Credential | Database role | Where it can live | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Publishable Key | `anon` | Frontend-safe | Still constrained by GRANT/RLS. |\n| User access token | `authenticated` | SDK-managed frontend session | Represents a real logged-in user. |\n| API Key | `service_role` | Backend / trusted tooling only | Bypasses RLS; never expose to browser code. Treat any leak as a serious credential compromise and rotate/revoke it via `manageAppAuth(action=\"deleteApiKey\")` immediately. |\n\n## `auth.users` — the built-in account table","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"903a9f18e7222d4c1e39fcf76dec31bef3fd46b6332f4bc5bc823999d287548b","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":144,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-b8a5996f9e2e4fd38ac234079f82b005","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/http-api.md","start_line":26,"end_line":null},"finding":"access token","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"| Credential | Database role | Where it can live | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Publishable Key | `anon` | Frontend-safe | Still constrained by GRANT/RLS. |\n| User access token | `authenticated` | SDK-managed frontend session | Represents a real logged-in user. |\n| API Key | `service_role` | Backend / trusted tooling only | Bypasses RLS; never expose to browser code. Treat any leak as a serious credential compromise and rotate/revoke it via `manageAppAuth(action=\"deleteApiKey\")` immediately. |\n\n## `auth.users` — the built-in account table","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"903a9f18e7222d4c1e39fcf76dec31bef3fd46b6332f4bc5bc823999d287548b","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/http-api.md","start_line":26,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-efca8a31e7ed4a1c8dc2659cc04ea340","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/web-development/frameworks.md","start_line":124,"end_line":149},"finding":null,"explanation":"This is a real vulnerability in the guidance: the NestJS AuthGuard is presented as token verification, but it only checks for the presence of a Bearer token and then trusts it by assigning `request.user = { token }`. Any attacker can supply an arbitrary token string and gain access to routes protected by this guard if downstream code assumes the guard performed authentication.","remediation":"Do not treat token presence as verification. Replace the sample with actual validation logic using a trusted server-side mechanism: verify the token signature/claims with a supported CloudBase server flow, or send the token to a backend/cloud function/HTTP API that validates it before granting access. Update the example and comments so the guard explicitly denies access unless verification succeeds, and avoid setting `request.user` from untrusted input prior to validation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/web-development/frameworks.md","start_line":124,"end_line":149}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-ca16606a80a148e9945323dab95517b1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The main `description` says to use this skill for a very wide range of activities including develop, design, build, deploy, debug, migrate, and troubleshoot across many platforms and technologies. Although scoped to CloudBase, the trigger surface is still extremely broad and lacks concrete exclusion examples beyond a few negatives, increasing the chance of unintended invocation for general-purpose development requests that merely mention one listed term.","remediation":"Narrow the activation description to a smaller set of primary use cases, or provide an explicit trigger list with stronger constraints and negative examples. For example, require both a CloudBase-specific signal and a task type, and clarify when sibling skills should be preferred instead of this top-level skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-07e591935f0d4440a47ed6b586f6bdfd","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":81,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs users to run `npx skills add tencentcloudbase/cloudbase-skills` without pinning an exact package version. Because `npx` resolves the latest published package at execution time, a compromised upstream release or typo-squatted dependency could execute attacker-controlled code on the user's machine. In a security-sensitive agent skill, install commands are especially risky because they are likely to be copied verbatim.","remediation":"Pin the exact package and, ideally, integrity-verify it before use, for example by specifying an exact version (`npx skills@<version> add tencentcloudbase/cloudbase-skills@<version>`) or replacing ephemeral `npx` execution with a reviewed, locked installation path. Document trusted package sources and prefer reproducible install instructions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":81,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-d25b76378a7045a6b0aef82a134dd2d9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":150,"end_line":155},"finding":null,"explanation":"The derived activation triggers include broad natural-language phrases such as 'health check', 'troubleshooting', 'frontend interface', 'prototype', 'requirements', and 'tasks.md'. These phrases are common in everyday software work and, without mandatory CloudBase-specific gating in the trigger text itself, could cause the skill to activate for unrelated projects.","remediation":"Make each trigger explicitly require CloudBase context in the phrase or add negative examples showing non-CloudBase uses that should not activate the skill. Prefer narrower trigger formulations like 'CloudBase health inspection' or 'CloudBase spec workflow' instead of generic development language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":150,"end_line":155}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-67f5ed2ad11d48bf9f17d26a002a19a6","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":170,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The recommended command `npx plugins add TencentCloudBase/cloudbase-plugin -y --scope user` invokes tooling and fetches code without a pinned version. This creates a supply-chain execution path where future package changes, account compromise, or dependency poisoning can lead to arbitrary code execution under the user's account. The risk is amplified because this instruction is part of the primary setup flow for enabling management and deployment capabilities.","remediation":"Pin exact versions for both the `plugins` runner and the CloudBase plugin, and prefer installation methods backed by a lockfile or marketplace identity verification. If possible, provide signed release references, checksums, or a deterministic package manager workflow instead of bare `npx` execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":170,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-efdb1755898147708b8f0d04ce67c5cb","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":171,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"`npx mcporter list | grep cloudbase` relies on an unpinned `mcporter` package resolution if the binary is not already installed locally. While this appears to be a diagnostic step, `npx` may still download and execute the latest package, exposing users to the same supply-chain risk as other unpinned commands. Since the command is framed as a verification step, users may execute it with less scrutiny.","remediation":"Avoid `npx` for verification commands unless the package version is pinned exactly. Prefer invoking an already-installed binary, or document a pinned package invocation such as `npx mcporter@<exact-version> list` after users install that version through a controlled process.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":171,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-058619c5047e4f7b80b8d6a7a2b362aa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":308,"end_line":308},"finding":null,"explanation":"The UI-related signal is very common in ordinary frontend requests and is not inherently specific to CloudBase. Because this skill should not be used for non-CloudBase or pure frontend work, such a generic trigger can cause inappropriate activation and mislead the agent into applying CloudBase workflows where they do not belong.","remediation":"Narrow the phrase to CloudBase-specific UI scenarios, for example by combining it with login/auth, Web SDK, mini program, or explicit CloudBase terminology. Introduce a requirement that at least one product-specific signal be present before UI-first activation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":308,"end_line":308}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-016e6d8cc4804bf88ea35ba4e0d442d2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":392,"end_line":392},"finding":null,"explanation":"This trigger appears too generic to reliably identify a CloudBase-specific scenario, so it may activate on unrelated user requests. Ambiguous activation expands the skill's reach beyond intended boundaries and can lead to irrelevant or harmful guidance if the agent assumes CloudBase context that is not actually present.","remediation":"Replace the generic phrase with more specific wording tied to CloudBase resources, products, or APIs. Require contextual qualifiers such as platform plus CloudBase terms, and test the activation set against non-CloudBase examples to reduce false activations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":392,"end_line":392}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-64c8d9aaa9e241909d0cd4efc7da2d6b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":397,"end_line":397},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger phrase near this line is broad enough to match many generic troubleshooting or support requests, which can cause the CloudBase skill to activate outside its intended scope. In an agent-routing context, this can misroute users into CloudBase-specific guidance, increasing the chance of incorrect actions, unsafe assumptions, or accidental use of privileged CloudBase operations.","remediation":"Tighten the signal by requiring CloudBase-specific co-signals such as 'CloudBase', 'TCB', '云开发', specific APIs, or platform markers before activation. Add negative guards for generic troubleshooting terms unless they appear alongside CloudBase identifiers, and prefer multi-signal matching over single broad phrases.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":397,"end_line":397}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-1faf5243921a480d88136f443acd75fe","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/ai-model-nodejs/references/custom-onboarding.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.moonshot.cn/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"callCloudApi(service=\"tcb\", action=\"CreateAIModel\", params={\n  EnvId: \"<envId>\",\n  GroupName: \"custom-<your-name>\",  // MUST start with \"custom-\" (e.g. custom-kimi, custom-openai-compat); never start with \"cloudbase\"\n  BaseUrl: \"<OpenAI-compatible endpoint, e.g. https://api.moonshot.cn/v1>\",\n  Models: [\n    { Model: \"<model name, e.g. kimi-k2.5>\", EnableMCP: true }\n  ],","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"eccc8a7991113a9d526700f2a4d495f71d2c735d691cb001d58ebeaa5ca81c36","occurrences":[{"file":"references/ai-model-nodejs/references/custom-onboarding.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-1faf5243921a480d88136f443acd75fe","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/ai-model-web/SKILL.md","start_line":201,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.moonshot.cn/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"callCloudApi(service=\"tcb\", action=\"CreateAIModel\", params={\n  EnvId: \"<envId>\",\n  GroupName: \"custom-<your-name>\",  // MUST start with \"custom-\" (e.g. custom-kimi, custom-openai-compat); never start with \"cloudbase\"\n  BaseUrl: \"<OpenAI-compatible endpoint, e.g. https://api.moonshot.cn/v1>\",\n  Models: [\n    { Model: \"<model name, e.g. kimi-k2.5>\", EnableMCP: true }\n  ],","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"eccc8a7991113a9d526700f2a4d495f71d2c735d691cb001d58ebeaa5ca81c36","occurrences":[{"file":"references/ai-model-web/SKILL.md","start_line":201,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-98ce192f89f04b0fabae2359723a9142","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/ai-model-nodejs/references/custom-onboarding.md","start_line":21,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document instructs users to supply a vendor API key into a programmatic onboarding call but provides no warning about secret sensitivity, storage, rotation, or least-privilege handling. In a developer skill focused on CloudBase onboarding, this omission can lead users to paste production credentials into logs, source files, chat transcripts, or insecure automation, increasing the chance of credential leakage.","remediation":"Add explicit guidance that `Secret.ApiKey` is sensitive and must never be hardcoded, logged, committed, or exposed client-side. Instruct users to store keys in a secrets manager or secure server-side configuration, rotate compromised keys, scope them minimally, and ensure onboarding calls occur only from trusted backend/admin contexts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/ai-model-nodejs/references/custom-onboarding.md","start_line":21,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-ca1c334fd810499fbfb0c9ec38fa28aa","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":85,"end_line":null},"finding":"never ask the user","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n- Automatically use `auth-tool-cloudbase` to check app-side auth readiness via `queryAppAuth` / `manageAppAuth`, then get the `publishable key` and configure login methods.\n- **Publishable key readiness (do not skip):** call `queryAppAuth(action=\"getPublishableKey\")`. If it is empty, call `manageAppAuth(action=\"ensurePublishableKey\")` first — new environments may not have one provisioned, and skipping this step leaves the frontend without a data-plane credential, surfacing later as gateway auth failures instead of an obvious missing-key error.\n- **Persist the key, don't hoard it in conversation:** after retrieval, write the publishable key to `.env.local` as `VITE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (create the file if missing) and read it in client code via `import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`. Never hardcode the key into source files, and never ask the user to fetch it from the console — fall back to the console link below only if both MCP calls fail.\n- If `auth-tool-cloudbase` failed, let user go to `https://tcb.cloud.tencent.com/dev?envId={env}#/env/apikey` to get `publishable key` and `https://tcb.cloud.tencent.com/dev?envId={env}#/identity/login-manage` to set up login methods\n\n### Parameter map","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2a644ae57a82432a9c11f5d754db924983a683a84fee66cb1a104939410d39e6","occurrences":[{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":85,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c4d186c1d7de4610a1a9a0780b104170","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":138,"end_line":164},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file states that when a user asks for account-system features, the login page must follow a preset contract and includes Chinese-language requirements such as '登录/注册/账号体系' and Chinese-only references like 'Requires 邮箱/短信验证码登录 enabled'. This can steer the skill toward a specific language/locale behavior without explicitly offering the user a language choice or documenting that the skill is region/language-specific.","remediation":"State that UI copy and language should match the user's requested locale, or explicitly say the Chinese phrasing is illustrative only. If Chinese-specific behavior is required for a region-specific CloudBase workflow, document that constraint and justification clearly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":138,"end_line":164}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bea8f4890a1d46bda65ba0dd75719018","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/auth-wechat-miniprogram/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":16,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"The guide recommends enabling traceUser tracking by default without any privacy or consent guidance. While not an exploit primitive by itself, this encourages collection of user access telemetry that may be personal data, creating compliance and unnecessary data collection risks if developers adopt it blindly.","remediation":"Change the recommendation to explain that traceUser should be enabled only when needed and in accordance with the app's privacy notice, consent model, and data minimization requirements. Add guidance on documenting the collection, limiting retention, and disabling tracking in environments where it is unnecessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/auth-wechat-miniprogram/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":16,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6bc9436aedee4a8982504d1110761d54","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/auth-wechat-miniprogram/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":45,"end_line":58},"finding":null,"explanation":"The examples explicitly log and return OPENID/APPID/UNIONID, which are persistent identifiers tied to a user account. Even though the guide later says not to expose OPENID to other users, the sample code normalizes leaking these identifiers into logs and API responses, increasing risk of unnecessary disclosure, retention in logs, and misuse by downstream code.","remediation":"Do not log raw identifiers in example code. Return only the minimum data needed (for example, a boolean like authenticated: true or a server-side user record ID), redact identifiers in logs, and add an explicit privacy note stating that OPENID/UNIONID are sensitive persistent identifiers that should not be exposed to clients or stored in logs unless strictly necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/auth-wechat-miniprogram/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":45,"end_line":58}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d61c5ed938914fa48aab3d1c30185772","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/calling-methods.md","start_line":42,"end_line":56},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes destructive operations such as `DestroyEnv`, `DeleteUsers`, and force-delete parameters like `BypassCheck: true` / `IsForce: true`, but the surrounding guidance does not explicitly warn users about irreversible deletion or data loss. Under the markdown-file criteria for SQP-2, descriptions of behaviors that could affect user data or system integrity should include clear warnings.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the destructive examples stating that these actions can delete environments, users, or resources and may be irreversible. Recommend explicit user confirmation and backup/verification steps before invoking `DestroyEnv`, `DeleteUsers`, `BypassCheck`, or `IsForce` operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/calling-methods.md","start_line":42,"end_line":56}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-e07d2786815e4d1ca760fce0adf838e6","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/calling-methods.md","start_line":77,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.github.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"   - **托管三处，国内用户优先 CNB**：仓库命名 `tencentcloud-sdk-<lang>`（`-python` / `-go` / `-java` 等）。CNB 上挂在 `cnb.cool/tencent/cloud/api/sdk/` 路径下，raw 直链格式是 `/-/git/raw/master/`（不是 `/-/raw/`，用错会返回 404 HTML 但 HTTP 200，极易误判）；GitHub raw 是 `raw.githubusercontent.com/TencentCloud/<repo>/master/`；Gitee raw 是 `gitee.com/TencentCloud/<repo>/raw/master/`。\n   - **目录规律**：除 Node.js 外都是 `tencentcloud/<service>/<version>/`；schema 文件就在该目录下（Python `models.py`、Go `models.go`、Java 同包 `<Action>Request.java`）。每个接口一个 `<Action>Request` / `<Action>Response` 定义，字段名、参数名（json tag / 注解）、类型、必填性、注释齐全；同目录的 client 文件（`<service>_client.py` / `client.go`）可确认该 service 的 Action 全集。\n   - **Node.js 特例**：按服务 npm 分包 `tencentcloud-sdk-nodejs-<service>`，types `.d.ts` 就是 schema；源码在 `tencentcloud-sdk-nodejs` 仓库 `src/services/<service>/<version>/` 下。\n   - **不确定语言或路径时**：先抓仓库根目录的文件列表（GitHub API `https://api.github.com/repos/TencentCloud/<repo>/contents/tencentcloud`）确认实际结构，不要凭猜构造 URL；各仓库根路径 `examples/` 有每接口调用示例。\n   - 已实测锚点（Python 与 Go 结构完全同构）：\n     `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TencentCloud/tencentcloud-sdk-python/master/tencentcloud/monitor/v20180724/models.py` → `CreateAlarmPolicyRequest` 结构体直接可读。\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"061abab0022b7a79cdf98b2721e4ad6d47cd4ad12584ecf052130ef51f05d966","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/calling-methods.md","start_line":77,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1cf28d59b72e459ba4933dd200d79c26","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/billing-charges-explained.md","start_line":1,"end_line":59},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents all operational guidance, triggers, and user-facing instructions exclusively in Chinese. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in can be a natural-language policy violation unless the locale restriction is explicitly justified.","remediation":"Add an explicit language/locale note stating that the skill is intended for Chinese-speaking users, or provide a language choice / translated variant so users are not forced into a single language without opt-in.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/billing-charges-explained.md","start_line":1,"end_line":59}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-cb9448ddd38a4ec4a48287906a13ae5c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/custom-domain.md","start_line":1,"end_line":274},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file's operational guidance, warnings, and instructions are all presented in Chinese, and there is no indication that the skill is region- or language-specific by design. Under the policy rule, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Provide a language choice, add an English version, or explicitly document that this skill is intended only for Chinese-speaking or China-region users and why that locale constraint is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/custom-domain.md","start_line":1,"end_line":274}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-3ef09181b34046aca646033373a805c9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/pg-storage-alarm.md","start_line":1,"end_line":102},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents all operational instructions exclusively in Chinese, and there is no indication that the user can choose another language or that the skill is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking audience. Under the policy rule, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Add a clear language/locale notice and offer an alternative language version, or explicitly document that this recipe is intended only for a Chinese-language/tencent-cloud-specific audience with justification.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/pg-storage-alarm.md","start_line":1,"end_line":102}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-d1a7d8fe22894b4e949022e2d76e8715","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-agent-connect.md","start_line":1,"end_line":107},"finding":null,"explanation":"The entire skill document is presented in Chinese and does not indicate that the user can choose another language or that the locale restriction is intentional and justified. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without opt-in is a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Provide a language choice, include an English equivalent, or explicitly document that this skill is intended only for a Chinese-language audience with a justified locale constraint.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-agent-connect.md","start_line":1,"end_line":107}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-11729151ff974ce5817d750ba0009688","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-agent-connect.md","start_line":23,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"The recipe instructs users to place a live environment API key directly into MCP configuration via environment variables and emphasizes convenience over secrecy, but it does not clearly warn that this exposes credentials in local config files, process environments, editor tooling, and backups. In this skill context, the issue is more dangerous because it is specifically about connecting production-like cloud environments to an agent, so accidental disclosure could grant unauthorized access to a tenant environment.","remediation":"Add an explicit credential-handling warning before any example that includes API keys. Recommend secret managers or OS credential stores instead of plaintext config where possible, require project-local ignored files, document rotation/revocation steps, and state that users should prefer the local auth callback flow when they must avoid exposing the key to users or storing it in readable config.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-agent-connect.md","start_line":23,"end_line":40}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4e939860ad9d49dcad0a7a6a4f0c6fec","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-agent-connect.md","start_line":54,"end_line":72},"finding":null,"explanation":"The CLI and callback flows describe logging in with an API key and explicitly mention writing credentials to a local credential file, but they do not prominently warn that credentials persist on disk after the session and may be readable by other local processes, users, backups, or endpoint tooling. This is security-relevant because the documented goal is to let an agent operate against a CloudBase environment, so persistent credentials can silently outlive the intended session boundary.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that CLI/toolbox login persists credentials locally, identify the storage location and expected file permissions, and explain how to inspect, remove, or rotate stored credentials. Prefer ephemeral/session-scoped auth where possible, document cleanup after use, and instruct users to avoid shared machines or to use OS-protected secret storage.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-agent-connect.md","start_line":54,"end_line":72}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0a89bc4aa08e4367b1b888fb6e671466","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-onboarding.md","start_line":30,"end_line":30},"finding":null,"explanation":"The recipe explicitly tells operators to persist a mapping containing `用户 ↔ EnvId ↔ ApiKey`, which normalizes storing plaintext API keys in an internal database without any guidance on encryption, secret-management, access controls, masking, or rotation. Because these API keys grant access to tenant environments, compromise of that mapping table or its logs/backups could directly expose customer environments and break isolation between users.","remediation":"Do not store plaintext API keys in general application tables. Replace this step with secure secret handling guidance: store keys only in a dedicated secrets manager or encrypt them with a KMS/HSM-backed key, restrict access by role, never log or display full keys, store only metadata or a fingerprint where possible, define rotation/revocation procedures, and document how to safely deliver the one-time key to the user.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-onboarding.md","start_line":30,"end_line":30}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-407361c8f4d04800be7cc97b0bc11b32","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-usage-and-recycle.md","start_line":27,"end_line":28},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document includes an irreversible environment-destruction operation and notes that it is '不可逆', but it does not define an explicit pre-execution confirmation or approval step in the procedure itself. In an operational skill for platform environment lifecycle management, that omission can lead an agent or operator to execute deletion prematurely, causing irreversible data loss and service disruption.","remediation":"Add a mandatory confirmation workflow before `DestroyPlatformEnv`, such as requiring a separate explicit user approval, a typed confirmation including the target `EnvId`, and a pre-checklist covering backup/export, dependency review, and cooldown/disable-first validation. Prefer documenting a safer sequence: disable environment first, wait/verify, export needed data, then require a second confirmation before destruction.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-usage-and-recycle.md","start_line":27,"end_line":28}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-314f388865cf496b881095e9eab151e6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-functions/references/operations-and-config.md","start_line":71,"end_line":79},"finding":null,"explanation":"The guidance tells the operator how to disable gateway routes, including the default static hosting route, but does not place an explicit warning immediately before the action that this can take public endpoints offline. In an operational skill, that omission increases the chance of accidental service disruption or denial of service caused by a user or agent following the instructions without realizing the blast radius.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning before the disableRoute examples stating that disabling a route immediately removes public access for matching traffic and may cause production outage. Require explicit confirmation of target domain/path, recommend verifying environment and current route mappings first, and suggest rollback steps such as re-enabling the route after validation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-functions/references/operations-and-config.md","start_line":71,"end_line":79}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9fe15e0a03014a719e7b5a2efff5c9e8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-functions/references/operations-and-config.md","start_line":168,"end_line":170},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document includes layer version deletion as a normal management action, while the surrounding context notes that layers are account-scoped and shared across environments. Without an upfront, action-level warning before delete guidance, an agent or operator could remove a version still used by other functions or environments, causing widespread breakage.","remediation":"Add an explicit pre-deletion warning that deleting a layer version can break any function in any environment bound to that version. Instruct users to enumerate bindings first, confirm no active dependencies, prefer deprecating and migrating consumers before deletion, and require explicit user confirmation for destructive layer-version removal.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-functions/references/operations-and-config.md","start_line":168,"end_line":170}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e7eb6bbdfdda413896b581af53a40f88","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-storage-web/SKILL.md","start_line":86,"end_line":121},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains multiple critical instructions and API usage notes in Chinese, including mode-specific upload guidance and return-shape details. Because the skill does not indicate that Chinese is optional or provide a user language choice, it effectively imposes a locale on readers and can violate language/locale policy requirements.","remediation":"Provide the same guidance in a single user-selected language, or explicitly offer bilingual content with a clear language choice. At minimum, translate the Chinese-only operational instructions into the primary document language or split them into labeled bilingual sections.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-storage-web/SKILL.md","start_line":86,"end_line":121}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-4e9a4bc244dd4298b56565154ae655fa","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-storage-web/SKILL.md","start_line":191,"end_line":null},"finding":"do not ask the user","explanation":"The instruction to automatically retrieve or create a publishable key, write it into `.env.local`, and proceed without asking the user encourages autonomous credential management and local file modification. In an agent setting, this can lead to unauthorized configuration changes, secret sprawl, or use of a newly provisioned key in a project the user did not intend to expose for browser-side access.","remediation":"Require explicit user approval before creating or retrieving publishable keys or modifying `.env.local`. Limit the skill to suggesting the required steps, display the exact commands or tool actions for confirmation, and verify least-privilege/scoping of any generated publishable key before use.","code_snippet":"\nInitialization rules:\n\n- **Publishable key auto-provisioning (do not ask the user):** browser-side storage requests are data-plane calls that require a publishable `accessKey`. Before writing client code, call `queryAppAuth(action=\"getPublishableKey\")`; if empty, call `manageAppAuth(action=\"ensurePublishableKey\")`; then write the key to `.env.local` as `VITE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (create the file if missing) and read it via `import.meta.env.VITE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`. Never hardcode the key into source files. Only fall back to the console (`https://tcb.cloud.tencent.com/dev?envId={env}#/env/apikey`) if both MCP calls fail.\n- Use synchronous initialization with a shared app instance.\n- Do not re-initialize in every component.\n- If the operation depends on user identity, handle auth before storage operations.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6c70454728b03185163a4a49ef0ee04594a078335fd27f5b237f14a877522ca9","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-storage-web/SKILL.md","start_line":191,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-9a2423ee80b44bac980c3741862a4c16","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/SKILL.md","start_line":17,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instruction says 'If the user does not explicitly specify which programming language to use, TypeScript must be enforced.' This is a natural-language language-choice policy constraint that forces a specific language rather than asking the user or presenting options, which fits the language/locale policy-violation category.","remediation":"Replace the hard default with a user-choice step, such as asking the user to choose TypeScript or Python when unclear, or clearly document and justify why TypeScript is the required default in this context.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/SKILL.md","start_line":17,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"TM3","finding_id":"finding-5717e0a75d6148e18e8d9b953f3ca70b","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Unsafe Defaults","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.76,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null},"finding":"debug_mode=True","explanation":"The documentation's 'all options' example enables `debug_mode=True`, which may encourage deployment with verbose logging enabled. In an authentication- and API-key-integrated agent service, debug logs can expose request metadata, identifiers, error details, or other sensitive operational context that aids attackers or leaks user data.","remediation":"Change the example to use `debug_mode=False` by default and clearly label debug logging as development-only. Document what may be logged in debug mode, ensure secrets/tokens are redacted, and gate debug mode behind environment-based non-production checks.","code_snippet":"    bot_id=\"bot_1234567890\",\n    api_key=\"sk-1234567890\",\n    base_url=\"https://api.coze.com\",\n    debug_mode=True\n)\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1650bab1cd470fbf9a7107efd5fbb53dfbaa67a115ac4c0ebb708941ac533d6e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a94c0adcf84c423d8ab04719020bf815","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":65,"end_line":65},"finding":null,"explanation":"The guide describes extracting user identity from JWT-backed request context and using it as Coze `user_id`, but does not clearly warn that user-linked data is being sent to an external hosted AI service. In a CloudBase integration context, this can lead developers to transmit personally identifiable or sensitive tenancy metadata off-platform without transparency, consent, or data-minimization controls.","remediation":"Add an explicit privacy and data-sharing notice stating what fields are sent to Coze, why, and under what legal/consent basis. Minimize transmitted identity data by using opaque pseudonymous IDs, avoid forwarding full JWT claims unless strictly necessary, and document retention/processor implications for external AI backends.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":65,"end_line":65}]},{"id":"TM3","finding_id":"finding-ef41d88c1b384b4ca3ef65fd12cdd3b2","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Unsafe Defaults","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":162,"end_line":null},"finding":"debug_mode=True","explanation":"The custom error handling example explicitly turns on `debug_mode=True`, again normalizing verbose logging around a service handling JWTs, user identifiers, and external API interactions. In production this can leak internal state, token-related error details, and integration behavior useful for reconnaissance or data exposure.","remediation":"Revise the example to default to `debug_mode=False`, with a comment that debug logging should only be used in local development or controlled staging. Add guidance for structured logging with redaction and for suppressing sensitive exception details in production responses and logs.","code_snippet":"    adapter = CozeAgentAdapter(\n        bot_id=\"your-bot-id\",\n        api_key=\"your-api-key\",\n        debug_mode=True  # Enable debug logging\n    )\n    return adapter\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1650bab1cd470fbf9a7107efd5fbb53dfbaa67a115ac4c0ebb708941ac533d6e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":162,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-ddcad0f7d49a4383a262af89c397140a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":217,"end_line":227},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example auth middleware accepts requests without a Bearer token and silently assigns them the shared identity `anonymous`. In an adapter that forwards `user_id` to the backend for conversation history and tenant separation, this can collapse unauthenticated users into one identity, causing cross-user data mixing or unauthorized access to shared conversation state.","remediation":"Do not assign a default authenticated identity when authentication is missing. Reject unauthenticated requests with 401/403, and only populate `state[\"__request_context__\"][\"user\"]` after successful token validation; if guest access is needed, isolate it with per-session random IDs and explicit authorization boundaries.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":217,"end_line":227}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-bb8a3324ae694dec96a733d0726db49e","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":317,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Docker image references without a specific tag (:latest is implicit) or digest (@sha256:...) can be silently replaced by a malicious image.","remediation":"Pin the image: image:tag or image@sha256:abc123","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"29d709b6d6f740878a261fda073a846b679bbcfc19ae4e177f80c70381b789b3","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-coze.md","start_line":317,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1aa236b3f6fe4b208cd68af4a6fc7ea7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":214,"end_line":243},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file describes memory persistence and shows conversation data being stored and retrieved via `conversationId`/`thread_id`, which affects user data retention and privacy. Under the markdown-file criteria for SQP-2, the documentation should explicitly disclose that conversation history and identifiers are persisted and may contain sensitive content.","remediation":"Add a clear warning in the Memory & Checkpointing section stating that checkpointers persist conversation content and IDs, and advise users to obtain consent, avoid storing sensitive data unnecessarily, and configure retention/access controls appropriately.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":214,"end_line":243}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-6d2c72ca2fdb46928e6121fd62fbf405","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":235,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST http://localhost:9000/send-message \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"conversationId\": \"user_123_conv_456\",\n    \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}]\n  }","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n```bash\n# Each conversation gets unique thread_id\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:9000/send-message \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"conversationId\": \"user_123_conv_456\",","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1a2c34edd5e93d274d44f7111915294b3b320a654862cf4569be07c9bf9682d8","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":235,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1710e09d5d624a20a14e0720004e7b3d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":245,"end_line":262},"finding":null,"explanation":"The guide presents a production persistence example using PostgreSQL, but it does not mention that user messages and related state may be written to durable external storage. For markdown documentation, this is a missing warning because the behavior can affect privacy and system data handling.","remediation":"Add an explicit note near the PostgreSQL example that persisted checkpoints may include user conversation history and metadata, and recommend encryption, access restrictions, retention limits, and disclosure to end users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":245,"end_line":262}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-1c63894d4bbb47089c529842e64231c7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":5,"end_line":10},"finding":null,"explanation":"Lines L005-L010 establish an absolute rule: always deploy Agent services with `manageAgent` and do not use `createFunction` or `manageCloudRun`. However, lines L398-L420 later present CloudRun as an alternative deployment path for agent workloads, which directly contradicts the earlier mandatory guidance rather than merely adding implementation detail.","remediation":"Make the documentation consistent by either softening the earlier prohibition into a default preference with exceptions, or removing the later CloudRun deployment instructions from this file and placing them in a separate guide.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":5,"end_line":10}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0d8f880ed3734ea583ad2eecfcc02c62","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":30,"end_line":37},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation explicitly shows structured logs and error context containing `user_id`, `conversation_id`, and later raw `input` values. In an observability reference, readers are likely to copy these examples directly into production systems, which can lead to unnecessary collection and retention of personal data or sensitive prompts in logs and telemetry backends.","remediation":"Revise examples to use redacted or pseudonymous identifiers and avoid logging raw inputs by default. Add explicit guidance on data minimization, redaction, consent/notice requirements, retention controls, and a warning that sensitive fields should be filtered before being sent to logs, traces, or error trackers.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":30,"end_line":37}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-00e7f0803e4041b8ad5594ee6368332e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":131,"end_line":136},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trace propagation example shows injecting trace headers into outbound HTTP requests without warning that metadata may cross service or trust boundaries. Even if trace headers do not directly contain secrets, they can enable correlation of user activity across systems and may expose internal topology or request linkage to external observability providers.","remediation":"Document the trust-boundary implications of context propagation and recommend propagating trace context only to approved internal or trusted services. Add configuration examples for disabling propagation to third parties, sanitizing baggage/custom attributes, and reviewing what metadata exporters send externally.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":131,"end_line":136}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-eb4eb791ccba4218948847dacaea65cb","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":328,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST http://grafana:3000/api/dashboards/import \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n```bash\n# Import dashboard\ncurl -X POST http://grafana:3000/api/dashboards/import \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d @dashboards/cloudbase-agent-overview.json\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"22077d4b3c7bda9f49d674aec922d0b6fc0c52e1d378ee169e322c123ad87c47","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/observability.md","start_line":328,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-61165f91a74f40a0875c5a6687f237b5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/recipes.md","start_line":67,"end_line":107},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown recipe describes storing and reloading conversation history in Redis and saving user messages for later use, but it does not mention any privacy, retention, or consent warning. Because this affects user data persistence, the documentation should explicitly disclose that conversations are retained across sessions.","remediation":"Add a warning in this section stating that conversation contents and identifiers are stored persistently, and advise implementers to notify users, define retention limits, and protect stored chat data appropriately.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/recipes.md","start_line":67,"end_line":107}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6c87858c8f93473e97b16015f0ddf5ea","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/recipes.md","start_line":316,"end_line":345},"finding":null,"explanation":"The recipe processes documents in the background, loads document contents, sends them to an agent for analysis, and saves results, but the markdown provides no user warning about delayed processing or storage/handling of document data. This is a data-affecting workflow that should be disclosed in documentation.","remediation":"Add a note explaining that submitted documents may be processed asynchronously, their contents may be analyzed by the agent, and results are stored, with guidance to inform users and handle sensitive documents carefully.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/recipes.md","start_line":316,"end_line":345}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1fd8f19aa7994eb397c125533fa2cebf","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/server.md","start_line":121,"end_line":123},"finding":null,"explanation":"The multi-agent example explicitly enables fully permissive CORS with allow_origins, allow_methods, and allow_headers all set to '*' without any warning or scoping. In a CloudBase/agent server context, this can let arbitrary websites invoke the agent endpoints from a victim's browser, increasing the risk of cross-origin abuse, data exposure, and unauthorized use when credentials or ambient browser auth are present.","remediation":"Replace wildcard CORS with an explicit allowlist of trusted origins, methods, and headers. Avoid using '*' in production, disable credentials unless strictly required, and add documentation warning that public agent endpoints should be protected with authentication, authorization, and origin restrictions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/server.md","start_line":121,"end_line":123}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-044c217f705e4af58a183ea6767f3771","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/storage.md","start_line":64,"end_line":101},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes examples for saving full conversations and user identifiers in persistent storage, which can affect user privacy and data retention. Under the markdown-specific warning rule, the description should disclose that conversation content and metadata may be persisted and should be handled with appropriate privacy safeguards.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the Conversation Storage section stating that messages and user metadata may contain sensitive information, should only be stored with user awareness/consent as appropriate, and should follow retention and access-control policies.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/storage.md","start_line":64,"end_line":101}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0d3cddcc15ae460585bd33e6c87a2000","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/storage.md","start_line":248,"end_line":261},"finding":null,"explanation":"The migration example describes transferring storage contents from Redis to PostgreSQL but does not warn that the operation may move user or system data across persistence layers. In markdown documentation, such behavior should include a disclosure about privacy, access control, and validating destination security before migration.","remediation":"Add a warning in the Migration section explaining that migrations may copy sensitive data, and recommend reviewing access controls, encryption, retention requirements, and taking backups before running migrations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/storage.md","start_line":248,"end_line":261}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2dda537ba02e4604be1928096d707c2f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/tools.md","start_line":47,"end_line":57},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents HTTP tools and later shows async requests and storing processed results, but it does not warn that tool inputs or retrieved data may be sent to external services or persisted. For markdown files, SQP-2 applies when descriptions omit warnings about behaviors affecting privacy or user data.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the HTTP and composition examples stating that tool inputs may be transmitted to external APIs and that some tools may store results, so users should review endpoints, authentication headers, and data-handling implications before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/tools.md","start_line":47,"end_line":57}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-1b68ff5a8cb545fc8ed52a8dce94b655","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/ai-model-wechat/SKILL.md","start_line":234,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.example.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"http_tool = HttpTool(\n    name=\"fetch_data\",\n    method=\"GET\",\n    url=\"https://api.example.com/data\",\n    headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer TOKEN\"}\n)\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"88f1946300c8ae45d5ea7e81f2b6d4309a13082e928b6f7d1215d273945a1431","occurrences":[{"file":"references/ai-model-wechat/SKILL.md","start_line":234,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-1b68ff5a8cb545fc8ed52a8dce94b655","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/tools.md","start_line":55,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.example.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"http_tool = HttpTool(\n    name=\"fetch_data\",\n    method=\"GET\",\n    url=\"https://api.example.com/data\",\n    headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer TOKEN\"}\n)\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"88f1946300c8ae45d5ea7e81f2b6d4309a13082e928b6f7d1215d273945a1431","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/tools.md","start_line":55,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-1b68ff5a8cb545fc8ed52a8dce94b655","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/tools.md","start_line":87,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.example.com/","explanation"