d '{\n    \"conversationId\": \"conv_123\",","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d6670a688a200e7d54ae89a4922325856abffe3729d4b2de759ae77949452741","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/server-quickstart.md","start_line":291,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-274e71bacc6c435f81732542e82aa70f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/server-quickstart.md","start_line":345,"end_line":381},"finding":null,"explanation":"The monitoring callback example prints model output, tool-call arguments, run IDs, and errors directly to the console without any redaction or warning about sensitive data handling. In real deployments, prompts, completions, and tool arguments often contain secrets, personal data, tokens, or internal business data, which could then be exposed through logs and downstream log aggregation systems.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning that callbacks may log sensitive data and should not be used unchanged in production. Redact or suppress secrets, PII, and tool arguments by default; provide a safe logging example that masks values, samples only metadata, and routes logs through structured logging controls with retention and access restrictions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/server-quickstart.md","start_line":345,"end_line":381}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9ffde868400d4fdf999660b906115a5e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/skill.md","start_line":108,"end_line":108},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill’s Quick Start explicitly configures `app.set_cors_config(allow_origins=[\"*\"])`, which permits any website to make browser-based cross-origin requests to the agent API. In an agent backend context that may expose chat endpoints, tool execution, or authenticated user context, this broad CORS policy can enable unauthorized web origins to interact with the service and increases the risk of cross-origin abuse if credentials or bearer tokens are used by clients.","remediation":"Replace the wildcard origin with a strict allowlist of trusted frontend origins, ideally environment-specific (development vs production). Document the security implications in the skill, include a safe-by-default example, and if credentialed requests are supported ensure `allow_credentials`, allowed methods, and headers are tightly scoped.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/skill.md","start_line":108,"end_line":108}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-fdab6931b71045c6ba3da5339d0b7f8d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":49,"end_line":76},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown documents a production setup that persists conversation state in Tencent CloudBase and extracts a user ID from the Authorization JWT, but it does not warn users or operators about data storage, retention, or privacy implications. Because SQP-2 applies to markdown files, omission of disclosure around behaviors affecting user data is in scope.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning in the documentation that CloudBaseSaver stores user-associated conversation state persistently and that the example reads identity information from JWTs. Recommend documenting retention, access controls, and privacy considerations before using this pattern in production.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/adapter-langgraph.md","start_line":49,"end_line":76}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-0039dfb2967b46e7850ea04ccb07466a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/agent-deployment.md","start_line":9,"end_line":12},"finding":null,"explanation":"Lines L009-L010 state 'Do NOT use createFunction or manageCloudRun for Agent deployment' as a blanket rule. Later, lines L102-L126 explicitly describe cases where CloudRun should be used and provide a Dockerfile for that deployment path, which directly contradicts the earlier instruction.","remediation":"Revise the earlier prohibition to clarify that manageAgent is the default/preferred path, while CloudRun is an exception for listed scenarios. Ensure the guidance is consistent across the document.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/agent-deployment.md","start_line":9,"end_line":12}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-ea17024a3b1248dda5bbcd7a0c5c4a87","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/server-quickstart.md","start_line":397,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.openai.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"| Variable | Required | Purpose |\n|----------|----------|---------|\n| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | ✅ | OpenAI API key or compatible service key |\n| `OPENAI_BASE_URL` | ✅ | API base URL, e.g. `https://api.openai.com/v1` |\n| `OPENAI_MODEL` | ✅ | Model name, e.g. `gpt-4o` or `gpt-3.5-turbo` |\n| `LOG_LEVEL` | ❌ | Log level: `trace`/`debug`/`info`/`warn`/`error`/`fatal` (default: `info`) |\n| `ENABLE_CORS` | ❌ | Set to `true` to enable CORS (local dev only) |","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"49130770b598873cb46b4c0a98b1cf27c95fe909d4c07e88c505e6f0a11eb2bf","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/server-quickstart.md","start_line":397,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-ea17024a3b1248dda5bbcd7a0c5c4a87","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/agent-deployment.md","start_line":97,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.openai.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"| Variable | Required | Purpose |\n|----------|----------|---------|\n| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | ✅ | OpenAI API key or compatible service key |\n| `OPENAI_BASE_URL` | ✅ | API base URL, e.g. `https://api.openai.com/v1` |\n| `OPENAI_MODEL` | ✅ | Model name, e.g. `gpt-4o` or `gpt-3.5-turbo` |\n| `LOG_LEVEL` | ❌ | Log level: `trace`/`debug`/`info`/`warn`/`error`/`fatal` (default: `info`) |\n| `ENABLE_CORS` | ❌ | Set to `true` to enable CORS (local dev only) |","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"49130770b598873cb46b4c0a98b1cf27c95fe909d4c07e88c505e6f0a11eb2bf","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/agent-deployment.md","start_line":97,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e87c29398af84fb984b72b295a8fb1ca","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/server-quickstart.md","start_line":113,"end_line":140},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents enabling console and OTLP observability exporters, including a hosted Langfuse endpoint, but does not warn that request/trace data may be transmitted to third-party services. For a skill description, this omission matters because observability can affect privacy and system data handling.","remediation":"Add a brief warning in the Observability section stating that enabling exporters may send request metadata, prompts, traces, or other telemetry to external systems, and advise users to review/redact sensitive data before configuring remote endpoints.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/ts/server-quickstart.md","start_line":113,"end_line":140}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-cb508457cd804408aa1b2ae2529c88c5","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"63ed24f50a1ab74b4c5a21bd4095955f7f0d6b941ed8d885de44dc47c62be807","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-290a608aa5b84dc0995c5df6b0368b9f","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":136,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"The documentation recommends `tcb app delete ... --yes`, which suppresses interactive confirmation for an irreversible destructive action. In an agent-driven or CI/CD context, this lowers the safety barrier and can enable accidental or improperly authorized deletion of applications and all versions if parameters are wrong or user intent is misinterpreted.","remediation":"Require an explicit safety precondition before documenting or invoking non-interactive deletion, such as mandatory `--dry-run` output review, exact app-name matching, and a stronger warning that `--yes` should only be used in tightly controlled automation with validated environment IDs and approval gates.","code_snippet":"# Interactive confirmation\ntcb app delete my-app --env-id <envId>\n\n# Skip confirmation (CI/CD)\ntcb app delete my-app --env-id <envId> --yes\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":136,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-fb290eacdb17462d9dbdbd8de3501da5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":249,"end_line":259},"finding":null,"explanation":"The section heading and guidance from L249-L259 are written in Chinese, while the rest of the document is predominantly in English. This creates a language policy issue because the skill content forces a specific language for important operational warnings without user opt-in or a documented regional justification.","remediation":"Provide this section in the document's primary language as well, or explicitly state that the skill/documentation is intended for Chinese-speaking users only. Alternatively, offer bilingual content or a clear language-selection mechanism.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":249,"end_line":259}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-6c268849f8ed4156a83424741c0acb78","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":14,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"26790e7b1fb893d5f629b6f37d55e6a291bd75d2c63742e22ff50da90b50eedb","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":14,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-6c268849f8ed4156a83424741c0acb78","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/tooling-fallback.md","start_line":117,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"26790e7b1fb893d5f629b6f37d55e6a291bd75d2c63742e22ff50da90b50eedb","occurrences":[{"file":"references/tooling-fallback.md","start_line":117,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-e893a3bc86f64b338fb5d62bca0cb850","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":663,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"--config-file <path>     # Use a specific cloudbaserc file\n--verbose                # Verbose logging (add when debugging)\n--json                   # Machine-readable output (per command)\n--yes                    # Skip confirmation prompts (CI)\n--version                # Print tcb version\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/core.md","start_line":663,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-36524aa76eb34080b669f03d17576f75","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/hosting.md","start_line":142,"end_line":152},"finding":null,"explanation":"Lines L118-L120 clearly say `hosting list` has no `--limit` / `--offset` and that passing them fails as unknown options. The Common Options table at L151-L152 then documents those flags as available, which actively contradicts the earlier guidance and can cause users to invoke unsupported behavior.","remediation":"Remove `-l, --limit` and `--offset` from the Hosting common-options table, or clearly scope them to commands where they are actually supported. Keep the documentation consistent with the earlier warning that `hosting list` does not accept these flags.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/hosting.md","start_line":142,"end_line":152}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-335d9b8398b24a0fb131a3cfe97994ad","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/logs.md","start_line":3,"end_line":4},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document promotes a single command for searching logs across functions, auth, gateway, database, workflow, model, and LLM traces, but gives no caution that these sources can contain sensitive data such as credentials, tokens, personal data, prompts, or access metadata. In a troubleshooting skill, that omission can normalize broad log access and indiscriminate sharing or querying of sensitive operational data, increasing the chance of privacy leakage or overbroad access.","remediation":"Add explicit security guidance near the introduction and examples: warn that logs may contain secrets, personal data, prompts, auth events, and access records; instruct users to follow least-privilege access, minimize query scope by module/time/env, and avoid copying raw sensitive logs into tickets or chats. Include redaction guidance and examples of safe handling for auth, gateway, and LLM-related logs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/logs.md","start_line":3,"end_line":4}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-041a9e85d5a541d9be2ae455b512398c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/logs.md","start_line":112,"end_line":113},"finding":null,"explanation":"The LLM trace-log example encourages querying `module:llm AND logType:llm-tracelog` without warning that trace logs may include sensitive prompt content, model outputs, user inputs, or other confidential interaction metadata. In an AI/CloudBase skill context, this is especially risky because users may treat the example as routine debugging guidance and expose regulated or proprietary data.","remediation":"Add a specific warning adjacent to the LLM trace-log example stating that trace logs may contain sensitive prompts, completions, and user content. Recommend restricting access, narrowing time ranges and filters, redacting before sharing, and disabling or minimizing trace logging for sensitive workloads where possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/logs.md","start_line":112,"end_line":113}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-fa2ba382e4134cdab937d2eb2d1e77cf","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":87,"end_line":null},"finding":"skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n- `-e, --env-id <envId>` — target environment\n- `--json` — structured output (use for automation)\n- `--yes` — skip confirmation for destructive/confirmation-gated operations\n\n> ⚠️ Use the kebab-case `--env-id`. The old camelCase `--envId` still resolves as a hidden deprecated\n> alias, but it prints `⚠️ --envId 已废弃，请使用 --env-id` on every call — do not generate it.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"dc5042bb58e6fe9c8a4b4901b478317aa266bbe711b5044a1f06d1aad1e0fa2d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/app.md","start_line":87,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-fa2ba382e4134cdab937d2eb2d1e77cf","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/cloudrun.md","start_line":52,"end_line":null},"finding":"skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n- `-e, --env-id <envId>` — target environment\n- `--json` — structured output (use for automation)\n- `--yes` — skip confirmation for destructive/confirmation-gated operations\n\n> ⚠️ Use the kebab-case `--env-id`. The old camelCase `--envId` still resolves as a hidden deprecated\n> alias, but it prints `⚠️ --envId 已废弃，请使用 --env-id` on every call — do not generate it.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"dc5042bb58e6fe9c8a4b4901b478317aa266bbe711b5044a1f06d1aad1e0fa2d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/cloudrun.md","start_line":52,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-fa2ba382e4134cdab937d2eb2d1e77cf","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/cloudrun.md","start_line":370,"end_line":null},"finding":"skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n- `-e, --env-id <envId>` — target environment\n- `--json` — structured output (use for automation)\n- `--yes` — skip confirmation for destructive/confirmation-gated operations\n\n> ⚠️ Use the kebab-case `-