ocation":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/mysql.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null},"finding":"skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n- `-e, --env-id <envId>` — target environment\n- `--json` — structured output (use for automation)\n- `--yes` — skip confirmation for destructive/confirmation-gated operations\n\n> ⚠️ Use the kebab-case `--env-id`. The old camelCase `--envId` still resolves as a hidden deprecated\n> alias, but it prints `⚠️ --envId 已废弃，请使用 --env-id` on every call — do not generate it.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"dc5042bb58e6fe9c8a4b4901b478317aa266bbe711b5044a1f06d1aad1e0fa2d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/mysql.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-fa2ba382e4134cdab937d2eb2d1e77cf","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/permission.md","start_line":256,"end_line":null},"finding":"skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n- `-e, --env-id <envId>` — target environment\n- `--json` — structured output (use for automation)\n- `--yes` — skip confirmation for destructive/confirmation-gated operations\n\n> ⚠️ Use the kebab-case `--env-id`. The old camelCase `--envId` still resolves as a hidden deprecated\n> alias, but it prints `⚠️ --envId 已废弃，请使用 --env-id` on every call — do not generate it.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"dc5042bb58e6fe9c8a4b4901b478317aa266bbe711b5044a1f06d1aad1e0fa2d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-cli/references/permission.md","start_line":256,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-aa0f1edb258645a79022855cac42cf22","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/RULES_INDEX.md","start_line":26,"end_line":209},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents the substantive rule descriptions in Chinese throughout multiple sections, with no indication that language selection is optional or that the skill is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking region or audience. Under the policy-violation category, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language locale policy issue.","remediation":"Add an explicit language/locale note explaining that the skill is intended only for a Chinese-language context, or provide bilingual/translated rule descriptions so users can choose their preferred language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/RULES_INDEX.md","start_line":26,"end_line":209}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-1a1350ffce8046839d2ddabfa5e55ca0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/lint-rules/README.md","start_line":449,"end_line":450},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation table lists `PG-CR005 | error | PG 模式下存储上传缺少 storage.objects RLS 配置`, implying the lint script detects this condition. However, the code defines and calls checks through `checkSensitiveRuntimeEcho` and never defines any `check...` function or `record()` path for `PG-CR005`, so the documented intent contradicts actual behavior.","remediation":"Either implement a real `PG-CR005` check in the script and invoke it from main, or remove/update the README entry so the documented rule set exactly matches implemented checks.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/lint-rules/README.md","start_line":449,"end_line":450}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-a8272022b8194ec2a3c6adeb404d33de","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/cross-cutting/AUTH001.md","start_line":1,"end_line":57},"finding":null,"explanation":"The entire rule document is written in Chinese and presents normative guidance without any indication that the skill supports multiple languages or is intentionally restricted to a Chinese-speaking context. This can constitute a language/locale policy violation because it implicitly forces a specific language on users without opt-in.","remediation":"Add an explicit language/locale note justifying the Chinese-only scope, or provide bilingual/multilingual content or a user-selectable language option in the surrounding skill documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/cross-cutting/AUTH001.md","start_line":1,"end_line":57}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-2e35799b7a984796b7a25691ddde2a09","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/cross-cutting/SKILL001.md","start_line":1,"end_line":37},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains operational guidance only in Chinese, which effectively imposes a specific language on users or reviewers. Under the policy, forcing a language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy violation unless the locale restriction is explicitly documented and justified.","remediation":"Provide an explicit language choice or add a parallel English version. If the skill is intentionally Chinese-only, document the locale constraint and justification clearly in the file.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/cross-cutting/SKILL001.md","start_line":1,"end_line":37}]},{"id":"AS3","finding_id":"finding-8f992901a8dd4b1593ba431f4c3b012f","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Skill Enumeration","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/cross-cutting/SKILL001.md","start_line":31,"end_line":null},"finding":"skills/xxx/SKILL.md","explanation":"Skill enumerates or reads other installed skills. Access to other skills' SKILL.md files or the skills directory reveals prompt instructions, capabilities, and secrets that should be invisible to peer skills.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that list or read other skills' files or directories. Skills should operate independently; cross-skill access is a privilege escalation.","code_snippet":"## 修复指引\n\n1. 调用 `searchKnowledgeBase(mode=\"skill\", skillName=\"xxx\")`\n2. 从返回结果中提取 `absolute path`（如 `/Users/.../.claude/skills/xxx/SKILL.md`）\n3. 执行 `Read` 工具，传入该绝对路径\n4. 阅读完整内容后再写代码\n","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5bbc6b59ac67b37bfce0c0643a53433191891badfaedd46662e00287b20f5ea1","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/cross-cutting/SKILL001.md","start_line":31,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e2355ed1558649668d8a889977dcc0f4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/postgresql/PG-CR001.md","start_line":1,"end_line":61},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains all user-facing guidance in Chinese and does not indicate that the user can choose another language. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without opt-in is a natural-language policy concern unless the locale constraint is explicitly justified.","remediation":"Add a note offering language choice or provide a translated version (for example, Chinese and English). If this rule is intentionally limited to a Chinese-language audience, document that scope and justification explicitly near the top of the file.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/postgresql/PG-CR001.md","start_line":1,"end_line":61}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-b98a3393e3f6449d92dea1a62d1d862e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/postgresql/PG-CR004.md","start_line":1,"end_line":63},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown rule file presents all instructional content in Chinese, including the title, guidance, and remediation text. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in or documented regional justification is a natural-language policy concern.","remediation":"Provide a language choice, add an English version, or explicitly document that this skill is intended only for a Chinese-language or region-specific audience and why that constraint is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-code-review/references/rules/postgresql/PG-CR004.md","start_line":1,"end_line":63}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2498975d794646e1b644b2a57e51002c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-in-wechat-miniprogram/crud-operations.md","start_line":282,"end_line":365},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document includes several permanent deletion examples such as direct `.remove()` calls and batch deletes without accompanying confirmation, dry-run, rollback, or safety-warning guidance. In a developer-facing CRUD reference, this can normalize unsafe destructive patterns and increase the chance that users copy them into production flows where accidental or overbroad deletes cause data loss.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings before destructive examples, recommend confirmation UX for user-triggered deletes, and prefer soft-delete patterns by default. Include safeguards such as narrowing predicates, previewing affected record counts, requiring ownership/authorization checks, and documenting backup/recovery or transaction-based rollback options for bulk deletions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-in-wechat-miniprogram/crud-operations.md","start_line":282,"end_line":365}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-10ea5afa6f1746c6b3880ca1190c65c2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-in-wechat-miniprogram/geolocation.md","start_line":60,"end_line":95},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document provides concrete examples for collecting, storing, and querying precise user location data but omits any warning about user consent, minimization, retention, or applicable privacy obligations. In a developer-facing CloudBase skill, this can normalize implementation of location tracking without safeguards, increasing the chance that downstream apps process sensitive geolocation data unlawfully or excessively.","remediation":"Add explicit privacy guidance alongside the examples: require informed user consent before collecting location, explain platform/legal obligations, recommend collecting only the minimum precision and duration necessary, and suggest documenting retention/deletion policies. Update code snippets to show consent checks, graceful denial handling, and where possible use coarse location, anonymization, or server-side access controls for location data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-in-wechat-miniprogram/geolocation.md","start_line":60,"end_line":95}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-49481ee0c3c8418bace0526354619c38","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/crud-operations.md","start_line":433,"end_line":445},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes an example function that deletes all archived items with `.remove()` and immediately invokes it, but the surrounding documentation does not warn that the operation is permanent or suggest confirmation before running it. For markdown files, destructive behaviors that affect user data should be disclosed clearly.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the batch delete example that it permanently removes matching documents, and recommend a confirmation step, backup, or soft-delete approach before executing it in production.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/crud-operations.md","start_line":433,"end_line":445}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-00d3881e3af545489c614278f5e75d86","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/crud-operations.md","start_line":536,"end_line":571},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example class exposes `deleteTodo()` and `deleteCompleted()` using `.remove()`, and the usage section calls both methods, but the documentation does not prominently warn that these actions permanently delete records. In markdown documentation, destructive operations should include a clear caution about data loss or safer alternatives.","remediation":"Add a warning that these delete methods permanently remove documents, and suggest confirmation prompts, backups, or using the documented soft-delete pattern for important data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/crud-operations.md","start_line":536,"end_line":571}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-fa4d3045ddd04ba597d49e1c8b74e188","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/geolocation.md","start_line":60,"end_line":95},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation encourages storing precise user geolocation data and running location queries without mentioning consent, minimization, retention, or access control. In a CloudBase context, this can lead developers to collect and expose sensitive location data in ways that create privacy, compliance, and user-safety risks if misconfigured or over-collected.","remediation":"Add explicit privacy guidance near the storage examples: obtain user consent, collect only necessary precision, define retention limits, restrict reads/writes with security rules, and avoid storing precise coordinates unless required. Include a note to anonymize or coarsen location data where possible and to document lawful basis and regional compliance requirements.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/geolocation.md","start_line":60,"end_line":95}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-d3d0183b279943c7a0f49f0901324236","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/geolocation.md","start_line":223,"end_line":255},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example is logically incorrect: it claims to test whether a user point lies inside a store polygon, but applies geoWithin to the deliveryZone field using a Point as the query geometry. That can cause developers to implement broken delivery-boundary checks, leading to incorrect authorization or business-logic decisions such as allowing or denying service to the wrong users.","remediation":"Rewrite the example to use the correct geospatial predicate for point-in-polygon checks according to CloudBase semantics. For example, query the polygon field with the proper operator/geometry combination supported by the SDK, and add a short note clarifying directionality of geoWithin/geoIntersects with a tested example and expected result.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/geolocation.md","start_line":223,"end_line":255}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-66a3a79b50564ae7819c77f98d2dfd28","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":100,"end_line":null},"finding":"assume permission","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n### Using MCP Tool `managePermissions`\n\n**Important:** When developing applications that need permission control, you **MUST** call `managePermissions(action=\"updateResourcePermission\")` to configure database security rules. Do not assume permissions are already configured.\n\nCompatibility note:\n- Canonical plugin name: `permissions`","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c2c8af535086993f79da6f4d5ee69982386580837b497145c3e208a0d133b4c4","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-document-database-web-sdk/security-rules.md","start_line":100,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-53e7bf22b0cc473680419700b176b538","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description says to use this skill when 'choosing the domestic or international endpoint, setting site, region, cloud mode, or plugin flags,' which are broad administrative phrases that could overlap with many ordinary CloudBase conversations. Although later sections narrow scope, the top-level activation text does not give explicit trigger boundaries or negative examples in the manifest itself.","remediation":"Tighten the manifest description to enumerate narrower trigger phrases or contexts, and add exclusions such as 'not for creating/changing cloud resources' directly in the invocation description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-ea46d7b834ba4a1dbaef793bcd91f709","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs users to run `npx @cloudbase/cloudbase-mcp@latest`, which pulls and executes code at runtime from the registry without a fixed version. This creates a supply-chain risk: a compromised upstream package, malicious publish, or breaking update could cause arbitrary code execution in the user's environment.","remediation":"Pin the package to an exact trusted version instead of `@latest` (for example `@cloudbase/cloudbase-mcp@2.36.0`), and prefer lockfile-backed installation or a vetted local install path. If possible, document integrity verification and release review before upgrading versions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"4294dbad2ab1eeba93fd1df225e9004c369486d4c3683d9d6bbfd0c8abdee818","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-d62e86ed167c45e48f78c1317431d9dc","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Using `npx mcporter` without a pinned version can execute whatever version npm resolves at call time, which may change over time or be compromised. In a security-sensitive tooling workflow, this expands the supply-chain attack surface because the tool is used to enumerate and invoke MCP servers.","remediation":"Use an exact version for `mcporter` in all examples, or require installation via a lockfile-managed project dependency. Document a trusted installation path and avoid implicit latest-version resolution in command snippets.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-3ec898f24c6149b8b7dcd067153fe257","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":84,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The command example `npx mcporter describe cloudbase --all-parameters` relies on an unpinned package resolution path, so the code being executed is not stable or guaranteed to be trusted. An attacker controlling or compromising the package supply chain could execute arbitrary code when users follow the documentation.","remediation":"Replace `npx mcporter` with a pinned version such as `npx mcporter@<exact-version>`, or instruct users to use a previously installed, version-locked binary. Maintain examples that align with a reviewed version policy.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":84,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-d0e24bf251dd44cb8b30bccec81de947","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":85,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example `npx mcporter list cloudbase --schema` again invokes an unpinned package, allowing unexpected code changes or malicious package substitution at execution time. Because the command is positioned as a preparatory step before tool use, users are likely to run it directly and trust it.","remediation":"Pin `mcporter` to an exact version in the example or reference a local installed binary from a dependency-managed environment. Add guidance to review and update versions intentionally rather than resolving the latest at runtime.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":85,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-bad217ddfff34e2595bda80c1a3a7152","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":91,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The command `npx mcporter call cloudbase.queryEnv action=list --output json` executes an unpinned package and then uses it to communicate with infrastructure-related tooling. This combination increases the practical risk of supply-chain compromise because users may run the command in environments containing credentials or access to cloud resources.","remediation":"Use a fully pinned `mcporter` version or a locally installed trusted binary, and prefer execution from a lockfile-controlled project environment. Add a note warning against ad hoc execution of unversioned registry packages in credentialed environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-mcp/SKILL.md","start_line":91,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-327c1820a4da49f89bd1ef21c0c6536b","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-functions/SKILL.md","start_line":119,"end_line":null},"finding":"Never ask the user","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n1. Treat Integration Center creation as a console-first workflow unless a public Manager SDK or Cloud API contract is confirmed in official docs.\n2. Use official `index.md` docs for console UI steps and credential fields; do not copy stale console screenshots or invent field names.\n3. Never ask the user to paste secrets into chat. Tell them to configure merchant and official-account credentials in the CloudBase console Integration Center form.\n4. Do not assume generated function names are fixed. `pay-common` and `offiaccount-common` are examples; ask for or inspect the actual function name before writing calls.\n5. Treat frontend payment success as UI feedback only. The authoritative payment state must come from server-side query results or payment callbacks.\n6. When extending generated functions, preserve credential environment variables and generated callback verification/decryption logic. Add business logic around order checks, persistence, idempotency, and fulfillment.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"86cf7205d81e4d6e63ee679308a8f57007d09e1e0736da94173d1e471f2bfc76","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-functions/SKILL.md","start_line":119,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-327c1820a4da49f89bd1ef21c0c6536b","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-wechat-integration/SKILL.md","start_line":50,"end_line":null},"finding":"Never ask the user","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n1. Treat Integration Center creation as a console-first workflow unless a public Manager SDK or Cloud API contract is confirmed in official docs.\n2. Use official `index.md` docs for console UI steps and credential fields; do not copy stale console screenshots or invent field names.\n3. Never ask the user to paste secrets into chat. Tell them to configure merchant and official-account credentials in the CloudBase console Integration Center form.\n4. Do not assume generated function names are fixed. `pay-common` and `offiaccount-common` are examples; ask for or inspect the actual function name before writing calls.\n5. Treat frontend payment success as UI feedback only. The authoritative payment state must come from server-side query results or payment callbacks.\n6. When extending generated functions, preserve credential environment variables and generated callback verification/decryption logic. Add business logic around order checks, persistence, idempotency, and fulfillment.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"86cf7205d81e4d6e63ee679308a8f57007d09e1e0736da94173d1e471f2bfc76","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-wechat-integration/SKILL.md","start_line":50,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-d60b5070e47c4acfbc43512898885bd0","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/cloudrun-development/SKILL.md","start_line":275,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Docker image references without a specific tag (:latest is implicit) or digest (@sha256:...) can be silently replaced by a malicious image.","remediation":"Pin the image: image:tag or image@sha256:abc123","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f706d8f82c796eb6bf1da144248a7f0bb6fd31c989efc44b807806f34c553433","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudrun-development/SKILL.md","start_line":275,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-9be7eb1ebba04422a3541b88b7de4bf1","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/cloudrun-development/references/image-deploy-troubleshooting.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Docker image references without a specific tag (:latest is implicit) or digest (@sha256:...) can be silently replaced by a malicious image.","remediation":"Pin the image: image:tag or image@sha256:abc123","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7fd7ddd197bf869c71d683afba0ae792f70d4295b918fd9b9f0a6fb918826a37","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudrun-development/references/image-deploy-troubleshooting.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-67ba3b80434143ff82ab4214218a40d3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/cloudrun-development/references/vpc-and-database.md","start_line":106,"end_line":106},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example deploy payload embeds a full plaintext `DATABASE_URL` containing a username and password directly in documentation and deploy config. Even though it is an illustrative placeholder, this pattern normalizes putting secrets into command payloads, logs, shell history, screenshots, and version-controlled config, which can lead users to handle real database credentials insecurely.","remediation":"Replace the example with a non-secret placeholder such as `postgres://<user>:<password>@<private-host>:5432/<db>` and add an explicit warning not to hardcode credentials in docs, source, or deploy JSON. Recommend injecting secrets through CloudBase secret/env management, rotating DB credentials, and redacting sensitive values from examples and logs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudrun-development/references/vpc-and-database.md","start_line":106,"end_line":106}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1ac9cdaa943b4ac78e00ba56d1e22587","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/data-model-creation/SKILL.md","start_line":106,"end_line":106},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instruction 'Convert Chinese business descriptions into clear English identifiers' imposes a specific language output requirement. This is a natural-language locale policy issue because it does not provide user opt-in, alternatives, or a documented region-specific justification.","remediation":"Revise the instruction to preserve the user's requested language where possible or explicitly offer a choice, such as using the user's preferred language for identifiers or asking whether English naming is desired.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/data-model-creation/SKILL.md","start_line":106,"end_line":106}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-6b5783d4c2094a48a3aaeb85760b603b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":73,"end_line":73},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs the agent to 'always default to Phone SMS Verification' for user authentication when no method is requested, which overrides user choice and injects a region-specific identity flow without consent. This can lead to inappropriate collection of phone numbers, poor fit for non-Chinese or privacy-sensitive deployments, and insecure architectural decisions if the default is applied blindly rather than selected through threat modeling and product requirements.","remediation":"Remove the mandatory default and replace it with a neutral clarification step: ask the user to choose an authentication method based on region, compliance, UX, and security requirements. Provide SMS verification only as one option among several, with explicit tradeoffs and applicability notes, and require confirmation before implementing it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":73,"end_line":73}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-e189bb935a184e328297666420aa3530","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST \"https://your-env-id.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/functions/YOUR_FUNCTION_NAME\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <access_token/apikey/publishable_key>\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"### Cloud Function Invocation Example\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"https://your-env-id.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/functions/YOUR_FUNCTION_NAME\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <access_token/apikey/publishable_key>\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\": \"张三\", \"age\": 25}'","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0acfff3ba17f4ecc0866bff0b484e05e1635dcc8dc7b7bbc8d1301859f5c3245","occurrences":[{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-a6bd24c95ed9416aa88b7ef08fbdfce1","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X GET 'https://your-env.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/rdb/rest/course?select=name,position&name=like.%张三%&title=eq.文章标题' \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <access_token>\"\n\n# After URL encoding\ncurl -","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n```bash\n# Before URL encoding\ncurl -X GET 'https://your-env.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/rdb/rest/course?select=name,position&name=like.%张三%&title=eq.文章标题' \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <access_token>\"\n\n# After URL encoding","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"12e65b72b0a2bac27d31be05f7d911e1f6cc2fd5b44a0ba0e8aebe8ea9900a64","occurrences":[{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-459cc6ab4f1d4e1998c0bf1a0c6498a8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":314,"end_line":318},"finding":null,"explanation":"The guide explicitly instructs agents to ALWAYS default to phone SMS verification and presents it as the recommended flow without user opt-in or consideration of user locale, privacy expectations, or alternative authentication methods. This can drive unnecessary collection of phone numbers, create privacy/compliance issues, and bias agents into a region-specific identity flow that may be inappropriate for the user or application.","remediation":"Remove the 'ALWAYS use' directive and replace it with neutral guidance that asks the user or developer to choose an authentication method based on requirements, region, and privacy constraints. Document phone SMS as one option among several, require explicit user/developer preference before selecting it, and note data-minimization and jurisdictional considerations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/http-api-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":314,"end_line":318}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-da594f05ba0443f4895934af1d288c3c","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":90,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document instructs users to execute `npx plugins` without pinning an exact package version. Because `npx` resolves and may fetch the latest package at runtime, a compromised upstream package, malicious new release, or dependency hijack could cause arbitrary code execution on the user's machine during setup.","remediation":"Pin the exact package/version for every executable package invocation, for example `npx @openai/plugins-cli@<exact-version> ...` or the documented exact package name and version. Prefer lockfile-backed installs or vendor-reviewed installation paths, and avoid `@latest` or unqualified `npx` execution in security-sensitive setup docs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":90,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-367124f67e6b4436bf328508c0d856fc","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":93,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This command uses `npx plugins` without an explicit pinned version, which means the executed code can change over time and may be fetched from the registry at the moment of execution. In a setup guide for developer tooling, that creates a realistic supply-chain execution risk affecting local developer environments.","remediation":"Specify the exact package name and immutable version required for the `plugins` CLI, and update the documentation to use that pinned reference consistently. If possible, recommend installation through a trusted package manager workflow with integrity verification rather than transient `npx` execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":93,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-c0a4a0654b4d4fdd9b1fc002e11f657d","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":99,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The reference to `npx plugins` is unpinned, so the command may execute whatever version is current in the package registry rather than a reviewed version. That exposes users to supply-chain compromise and inconsistent behavior, especially harmful in plugin-install flows that modify IDE integrations.","remediation":"Replace the unqualified `npx plugins` invocation with a fully qualified package name and exact version. Document a version update process so maintainers consciously review and bump the pinned version when needed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":99,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-685af6945b9d42ceac560c8fbbc67544","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":101,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Running `npx plugins` without version pinning allows remote package content to be selected dynamically at runtime. If the package or one of its dependencies is compromised, the user may execute attacker-controlled code while installing CloudBase integrations.","remediation":"Use an exact package/version pin for the plugin CLI and avoid floating installs in the documentation. Consider replacing transient `npx` usage with a preinstalled, locked dependency or signed distribution channel.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":101,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-4b68b7043df445e78e6270df1c6b4f82","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":116,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This `npx plugins` example is another unpinned executable dependency reference. In practice, such instructions normalize executing mutable third-party code directly from the registry, which is a common supply-chain attack vector.","remediation":"Pin the CLI package to an exact version and ensure all examples use the same reviewed release. Add guidance warning against running unqualified `npx` commands from documentation in production or enterprise environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":116,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-594fe1504a2c4c54abbbe2dedc9ec43d","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":118,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The doc tells users to run `npx plugins targets` without fixing the package version. That introduces arbitrary-code-execution risk from a mutable upstream package and undermines reproducibility for security-sensitive tooling setup.","remediation":"Document the exact package and version for the `plugins` CLI, and update examples to invoke that immutable version. Where possible, provide checksums, signed releases, or internal mirrors for controlled environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":118,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-09f6befa680f431e9db79a9d85598cec","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":121,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This unpinned `npx plugins` usage exposes users to execution of a future package version that the skill author has not reviewed. Since the command installs IDE plugins, compromise could cascade into broader developer-environment persistence or credential exposure.","remediation":"Pin the exact version of the `plugins` package and review plugin installation guidance for least privilege. Prefer deterministic installation instructions and avoid registry-resolved floating executables.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":121,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b213a0775f70489abd400dcf981278b0","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":123,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Another unversioned `npx plugins` invocation appears in the setup instructions. Repeatedly encouraging this pattern increases the chance that users execute malicious or compromised package contents from npm during routine setup.","remediation":"Standardize on exact version pins for all `npx`-executed CLIs in the file. If a versionless command must be shown, accompany it with explicit risk warnings and a safer pinned alternative.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":123,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-e75bdc054beb412a803286763c591f4d","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":156,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The MCP configuration launches `npx` with `@cloudbase/cloudbase-mcp@latest`, which explicitly opts into a floating package version. Any malicious release, typo/hijack event, or compromised maintainer account could turn IDE/MCP startup into arbitrary code execution on the workstation.","remediation":"Replace `@latest` with an exact reviewed version of `@cloudbase/cloudbase-mcp`. Maintain a documented upgrade cadence and verify new releases before updating the pinned version in examples.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9e97734885787657ab861319f29b1346d94b3d9d32539523a80ada9f50a3587d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":156,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-c7086cd046a14e34badc50dd71bb2f0f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":166,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `npx mcporter` command is unpinned, so users may execute whatever version npm resolves at runtime. Because mcporter is used to enumerate and invoke MCP servers, compromise could give an attacker code execution and access to local project context.","remediation":"Use a fully qualified package invocation with an exact version for `mcporter`. Prefer installation through a lockfile-managed dependency or an approved internal package mirror.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":166,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-7314ac3646754886a1906972bbba2815","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":182,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This configuration again relies on `npx` plus `@cloudbase/cloudbase-mcp@latest`, causing mutable code to run whenever the server is started. In MCP contexts, that is particularly sensitive because the process may access files, secrets, tokens, and IDE-mediated actions.","remediation":"Pin `@cloudbase/cloudbase-mcp` to an exact version and avoid `@latest`. Consider recommending local installation with a locked dependency version instead of transient fetch-and-run behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":182,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f6995b95921942b5b517971d5e20a04f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":188,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The quick-start `npx mcporter list` command is versionless and may fetch executable code at runtime. While less privileged than plugin installation, it still creates supply-chain execution risk on the developer machine.","remediation":"Document the exact package and version for the `mcporter` CLI. Encourage users to install a pinned version or run it from project dependencies rather than bare `npx`.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":188,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-8ebceb77eff04bd8a0c340b759f2c0a3","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":189,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This `npx mcporter describe` usage is unpinned, so a compromised registry package could run code before or instead of performing the intended inspection. Because the command is framed as required, users are likely to run it routinely without additional scrutiny.","remediation":"Pin the exact `mcporter` package version in the command examples. If possible, include a non-executable documentation alternative for schema discovery to reduce dependence on transient CLI execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":189,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f7bf8b8524414e15ae0e9628b95df5a9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":189,"end_line":189},"finding":null,"explanation":"The line includes a natural-language instruction in Chinese stating that `--all-parameters` must be added to obtain complete parameter information. This introduces a language-specific requirement in the skill content without offering the user a language choice or documenting a justified locale constraint.","remediation":"Rewrite the instruction in the document’s primary language or provide both languages with an explicit note that language choice is optional. If Chinese is required for a region-specific audience, document that scope clearly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":189,"end_line":189}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-452efe0252764351ae3d065a690feb6c","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":190,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example uses `npx mcporter` without an immutable version, which creates a mutable trust boundary at execution time. Attackers who compromise the package or dependency chain could execute code under the user's account.","remediation":"Replace versionless `npx mcporter` with a fully pinned package/version reference. Keep examples aligned to a tested CLI release and note the supported version range elsewhere in docs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":190,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-dbe1749127c943a58a31686bdf4e5ea3","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":191,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Calling `npx mcporter call ...` from documentation without pinning means the user is trusting whichever package version npm resolves on that day. That is a classic supply-chain risk and is unnecessary in stable setup guidance.","remediation":"Update the command to invoke an exact reviewed version of the mcporter CLI. For repeated use, recommend installing the pinned CLI as a project or user dependency instead of bare `npx`.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":191,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-7bec01459d9b459a92ca332c5cee2887","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":192,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This generic `npx mcporter call` pattern is unpinned and therefore executes mutable remote code. Although it is a usage example, it still trains users into an unsafe installation/execution habit in a privileged development environment.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter executable version in the example and add a note to prefer local locked installs. Avoid demonstrating floating `npx` commands in security-conscious documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":192,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-e0df8717017940e68e54b9e755cd7648","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":199,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The auth status example uses an unpinned `npx mcporter` invocation. Any compromise in the CLI supply chain could expose authentication state, local config, or execute arbitrary code under the user's account.","remediation":"Use an exact package name/version for mcporter in the documentation and ensure users run a reviewed build. Consider an alternative invocation path using installed dependencies or signed binaries.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":199,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-84a67f61fcad41b49e40200b3d49747b","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":201,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This start-auth command depends on bare `npx mcporter`, which may fetch and run unreviewed code at execution time. Because it interacts with auth flows, compromise could misdirect users, capture tokens, or tamper with environment configuration.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter package version and document trusted distribution expectations. Avoid floating registry-resolved executables in authentication-related examples.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":201,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-eaa4033bf8224310a59b7811b2693e3f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":203,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The alias-resolution example again relies on unpinned `npx mcporter`. In a developer tooling guide, repeated use of mutable executables broadens the window for supply-chain attacks and reduces reproducibility.","remediation":"Provide exact-version invocation syntax for mcporter and keep it consistent across all examples. Optionally provide a shell variable or wrapper script so one reviewed version is reused everywhere.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":203,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-844346e2c3e64785945e4cac45680ed3","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":205,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Binding an environment via unpinned `npx mcporter` trusts whatever version npm resolves at runtime. A malicious package could alter environment targets or exfiltrate configuration while appearing to perform legitimate setup.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter CLI to a specific reviewed version and avoid versionless `npx` in examples. Add guidance to verify tool provenance before first use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":205,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-51aa7614ac364e7690a5a60dfd0d9dfd","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":207,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The login-config query example is another unpinned `npx mcporter` execution path. That makes local command execution dependent on a mutable third-party registry state, which is unsafe for admin or auth-related operations.","remediation":"Use a fixed mcporter version in the command and prefer a lockfile-backed install for operational workflows. Remove or minimize bare `npx` examples from sensitive sections.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":207,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-5a9df450c42e4c0c94c5b8bed405b2d5","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":209,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This patch-login-strategy example executes a versionless CLI from npm. Because it modifies auth behavior, compromise could have both local code-execution effects and configuration-tampering effects against the target environment.","remediation":"Pin the exact mcporter version and, if feasible, separate mutation examples from transient execution guidance. Encourage users to review and install trusted tool versions before performing admin actions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":209,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-ac742ca3a2b84dc6adf351c99e522452","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":211,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The publishable-key query example uses unpinned `npx mcporter`, exposing the user to arbitrary code execution from a mutable package source. Even read-oriented commands can be abused to harvest credentials, config, or local secrets.","remediation":"Pin mcporter to an exact version in the documentation and recommend local installation through controlled dependency management. Add a note that registry-fetched CLI execution should be treated as trusted-code execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":211,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-2328fe5938b340d29f921231af77f12f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":224,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The environment-package listing command uses unpinned `npx mcporter`, allowing execution of potentially unreviewed upstream code. As part of infra management guidance, this increases supply-chain risk for operators and developers.","remediation":"Specify an exact mcporter version and use that consistently across lifecycle-management examples. Consider publishing tested command snippets tied to specific tool releases.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":224,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-dc1181e75762470894ff600a621f1b3c","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":228,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The environment creation command runs through bare `npx mcporter`, which means a compromised CLI could execute arbitrary code and also manipulate resource-creation requests. Because this example performs provisioning, the blast radius includes both the local host and the cloud account.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter package to an exact version and require reviewed tool updates before use. For provisioning workflows, prefer signed binaries or internally mirrored packages with integrity controls.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":228,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-7e7889a1fad74ac5834491f5394bebcb","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":235,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Changing an environment plan via unpinned `npx mcporter` creates both code-execution and cloud-account change risk. An attacker controlling the CLI path could alter billing-sensitive operations or target the wrong environment while running arbitrary local code.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter version and avoid transient registry execution for billing or plan-management commands. Add explicit environment verification steps and use least-privilege credentials.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":235,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-6e43bc9f45e746898b02ced42503d828","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":238,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The renew-environment example relies on an unpinned executable CLI from npm. Compromise could lead to unauthorized renewal actions, altered parameters, or arbitrary code execution on the user's machine.","remediation":"Use a fully qualified exact mcporter version and prefer controlled distribution channels. Review all admin-action examples to eliminate floating executable dependencies.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":238,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b79ee3856d5d479892d69dbbb5e7bdd1","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":243,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The repeated `npx mcporter` status example remains a supply-chain execution risk due to lack of version pinning. In aggregate, the document makes unsafe transient execution a normal operational pattern.","remediation":"Pin the CLI version in every example and add one canonical installation section for a reviewed release. Reduce repeated bare `npx` usage throughout the doc.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":243,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-bce476adb4774f9084180b4486cf72d7","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":246,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This environment-binding example uses the same unpinned `npx mcporter` pattern. The risk is amplified slightly because the command influences active environment context, which a malicious CLI could silently redirect.","remediation":"Document a fixed mcporter version and include validation steps after binding to confirm the selected environment. Eliminate bare `npx` execution for context-changing commands.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":246,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-7a1027bcb57740989470335b07c72fb3","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":249,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The logout command uses unpinned `npx mcporter`, which still permits arbitrary code execution even though the nominal action is simple. Security-sensitive documentation should not rely on mutable registry resolution for executable admin tools.","remediation":"Pin the exact mcporter version and recommend users install or cache the reviewed release through managed dependencies. Keep auth/session commands on deterministic tool versions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":249,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f42c7c55cb8a467d9d578d26c446a18e","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":254,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Listing environments via bare `npx mcporter` leaves command execution dependent on the current npm registry state. This is a genuine but common documentation weakness that could expose local config or credentials if the package is compromised.","remediation":"Use an exact version for mcporter and prefer a previously installed trusted binary or local dependency. Add internal package mirror guidance for enterprise users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":254,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b1bd9d58ae3c41ce94ec59b6da8993c9","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":257,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The environment-info example remains unpinned and therefore subject to supply-chain execution risk. Because it queries runtime/backend details, a malicious CLI could also misreport state and mislead subsequent operator decisions.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter version and, where practical, suggest validating important environment data via an independent trusted console or API. Remove floating `npx` usage from operational inspection steps.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":257,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-c0b841914b984d1c88bc343171e2a415","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":260,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This alias-resolution command uses unversioned `npx mcporter`, again allowing runtime retrieval of mutable code from npm. The direct risk is local code execution; the indirect risk is returning manipulated environment identifiers.","remediation":"Pin the exact mcporter release in the example and maintain a documented approved-version list. Encourage users to verify resolved environment IDs before applying changes.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":260,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-53838c42623f459aa8f2454b1b43fdfc","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":264,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"866ee31b3429ad0d4cec30385df584cf6ba6c1c0e72f564946cb307be3d6366f","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":264,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-4682758a84a94e81b354b7c4e68d2bfa","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":266,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The same line also references `npx mcporter` without an exact version, which carries the same mutable-code execution risk. Because the document is instructional, users may still copy the shorthand reference into a shell.","remediation":"Replace shorthand mentions with a pinned package/version reference or point back to a single canonical pinned command definition. Avoid mentioning bare `npx mcporter` in user-facing docs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e31784003ab91a7b35b72c3dda0831aed8eaf98abc43c411cf97b947b2000b61","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":266,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f5d2c57ec07349a783ad6f4db897c27c","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":266,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The same line also references `npx mcporter` without an exact version, which carries the same mutable-code execution risk. Because the document is instructional, users may still copy the shorthand reference into a shell.","remediation":"Replace shorthand mentions with a pinned package/version reference or point back to a single canonical pinned command definition. Avoid mentioning bare `npx mcporter` in user-facing docs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":266,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-ea274398f8884db6b90b9207024d33fc","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":274,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The 'Important Rules' section instructs users to run `npx mcporter describe cloudbase --all-parameters` before tool usage, but the command is unpinned. Because it is framed as mandatory, this substantially increases the likelihood of repeated execution of mutable registry code.","remediation":"Pin the exact mcporter version in this required command and keep it synchronized with the tested server/tooling versions. If possible, provide an IDE-native schema-inspection path that avoids shell execution altogether.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":274,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-7cce74102cdf4385b82202595a877710","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":278,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The MCP-availability verification step uses bare `npx mcporter`, again exposing users to supply-chain execution risk from an unpinned CLI. Since this is a diagnostic prerequisite, many users will run it before any other safeguards or context checks.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter CLI version and provide a safer alternative such as checking the IDE's MCP panel first. Consolidate diagnostics around a reviewed, deterministic tool version.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":278,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-bfc41b336ef4475ea4641c61f2677e98","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":278,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The MCP-availability verification step uses bare `npx mcporter`, again exposing users to supply-chain execution risk from an unpinned CLI. Since this is a diagnostic prerequisite, many users will run it before any other safeguards or context checks.","remediation":"Pin the mcporter CLI version and provide a safer alternative such as checking the IDE's MCP panel first. Consolidate diagnostics around a reviewed, deterministic tool version.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"26790e7b1fb893d5f629b6f37d55e6a291bd75d2c63742e22ff50da90b50eedb","occurrences":[{"file":"references/mcp-setup.md","start_line":278,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-af73399a174a4d7ab983445b2f3817c2","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/minimal-web-baas-demo/SKILL.md","start_line":37,"end_line":null},"finding":"Do not ask the user","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"## Hard rules (align with Sites SessionStart Rule 5)\n\n1. **BaaS-first data path**\n   - **Schema / admin:** Prefer MCP management tools. Do not ask the user to create collections/tables in the console. If MCP tools are missing in this session, configure MCP for next time and use `tcb` CLI (`../cloudbase-cli/SKILL.md`) for equivalent schema/admin ops.\n     - NoSQL: `writeNoSqlDatabaseStructure` (create collection / indexes) + permission tools as needed; CLI: NoSQL commands in `cloudbase-cli`.\n     - PostgreSQL: follow `../postgresql-development-cloudbase/SKILL.md` (`queryPgDatabase` / `managePgDatabase` / migrations); CLI parity via `tcb db pg …` when MCP is unavailable.\n   - **Reads / writes:** `@cloudbase/js-sdk` in the browser.","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"53c32905e950cbdc0f915b81bab4262cf87077e93ee69f468581a690049d9c76","occurrences":[{"file":"references/minimal-web-baas-demo/SKILL.md","start_line":37,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-db6a5280ee59414c96f680012a5d3639","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/cloudbase-integration.md","start_line":1,"end_line":180},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file’s instructional content is exclusively in Chinese, including operational guidance for the coding agent, and does not provide an opt-in language choice or state that the skill is intentionally limited to Chinese-speaking users. Under the policy for natural-language violations, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is in scope.","remediation":"Add a clear note that the reference is intended for Chinese-language users or provide a bilingual version / language selection path. If the locale restriction is intentional, document the justification explicitly near the top of the file.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/cloudbase-integration.md","start_line":1,"end_line":180}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-34c010d3a5e54910b247940a38855458","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/cloudbase-integration.md","start_line":47,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/cloudbase-integration.md","start_line":47,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-34c010d3a5e54910b247940a38855458","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence