ull,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/cloudbase-integration.md","start_line":54,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/cloudbase-integration.md","start_line":54,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-cfd6ed2337cb426f91b2ff6898050d0d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/devtools-debug-preview.md","start_line":1,"end_line":179},"finding":null,"explanation":"The entire skill reference is written in Chinese and includes prescriptive instructions for agent behavior, but it does not offer any user choice of language or indicate that Chinese is optional. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without opt-in is a natural-language policy violation unless the locale restriction is explicitly justified.","remediation":"Add a clear note that Chinese is the default only for this reference, and require the agent to match the user's preferred language or ask for language preference when needed. If the skill is intentionally China-specific, explicitly document that scope and justification.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/devtools-debug-preview.md","start_line":1,"end_line":179}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c6e2eb2607894157aee2386807d1e5b7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/message-push-customer-service.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"L005-L007 使用“操作面（强制）”和“当前唯一支持路径”这类强制性表述，将技能操作限定在特定工具/环境路径，但全文未给用户提供语言或区域/locale 选择。按规则，若技能以自然语言强制特定语言/locale 且无用户 opt-in 或明确合理化说明，应视为政策问题。","remediation":"若该限制是工具链约束，请明确说明这是产品/平台能力限制而非语言/locale 强制；若涉及面向特定语言用户，请补充可选语言说明或要求在用户确认后再固定语言输出。","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/message-push-customer-service.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-ca790783daad481abc42ea933529201a","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/wxide-vs-cloudbase-mcp.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document recommends executing `npx skills add tencentcloudbase/cloudbase-skills -y` without pinning a specific package version. This creates a supply-chain risk because the latest published package is fetched at execution time, so a compromised or malicious future release could be installed unexpectedly. In a developer skill focused on CloudBase workflows, this is more dangerous because readers are likely to copy-paste the command directly into trusted development environments.","remediation":"Pin the exact package version in the command, for example by specifying an explicit version tag, and document how to verify package provenance or integrity before installation. Prefer a locked installer workflow or checksum/signature verification in documentation where possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"references/miniprogram-development/references/wxide-vs-cloudbase-mcp.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-ecc7c3c17a594d9a98b8e9f28e3b5506","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/ops-inspector/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description says the skill triggers on terms including \"诊断\" and \"troubleshooting\", which are generic phrases commonly used across many support contexts, not just CloudBase inspection. Although the description is CloudBase-focused, the trigger list itself does not include explicit exclusion conditions or negative examples to prevent overlap with unrelated debugging requests.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger list to CloudBase-specific phrases such as \"CloudBase 巡检\", \"CloudBase 告警解读\", or \"CloudBase 429 排查\", and add negative examples or scope limits stating that generic troubleshooting requests outside CloudBase should not activate this skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/ops-inspector/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-d21ffc40b7754500acf91108332d4d53","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/ops-inspector/references/fault-playbooks.md","start_line":1,"end_line":206},"finding":null,"explanation":"The playbook repeatedly instructs what to tell the user using Chinese-only response text and mixes Chinese symptom phrases throughout, but nowhere offers a language choice or states that the skill is intentionally limited to Chinese-speaking users. This creates a natural-language locale policy issue because it implicitly enforces a specific language without user opt-in.","remediation":"Document that the skill is explicitly China/Chinese-language scoped if that is intended, or add guidance to respond in the user's preferred language. If localized examples are needed, label them as examples and instruct the agent to adapt output language based on user preference.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/ops-inspector/references/fault-playbooks.md","start_line":1,"end_line":206}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-0cbe672f5e1f460694384d1c71ed8f33","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":218,"end_line":264},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill is primarily written in English, but this section switches to Chinese phrases such as 'URL 加 .md 可取 raw markdown 原文', '或', '通过', and '注意 range 是包含两端的分页' without any opt-in or documented locale requirement. That can violate language/locale policy because it forces part of the guidance into a specific language for all users.","remediation":"Keep the entire skill in one language by default, or explicitly offer bilingual content with a clear language choice. If Chinese is required for a region-specific audience, document that constraint in the skill description or activation contract.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":218,"end_line":264}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-cae4672105144558b2b5d31507f2213b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/app-workflow.md","start_line":74,"end_line":74},"finding":null,"explanation":"The guidance recommends using `drop table if exists ... cascade` in disposable environments or when a known schema is required, but it does not pair that advice with an explicit warning about irreversible data loss or a verification step before execution. In a workflow document for app repair and migration, this can lead users to destroy production or shared-environment data during routine troubleshooting or schema alignment.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning that destructive resets permanently delete data and must only be used in disposable or fully backed-up environments. Require a confirmation checklist before reset guidance, such as verifying the target environment, confirming backups, and preferring non-destructive migrations when any real user data may exist.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/app-workflow.md","start_line":74,"end_line":74}]},{"id":"SSRF3","finding_id":"finding-e69252c5075a4ebaabb2fd40a05d5e9b","category":"Server-Side Request Forgery","pattern":"Dynamic Request Target","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":128,"end_line":null},"finding":"fetch(`https://${","explanation":"Request target host is built from a dynamic or untrusted value. If the host is attacker-influenced, this enables SSRF to arbitrary internal or metadata endpoints.","remediation":"Do not build request URLs from untrusted input. Validate the host against an allowlist and reject internal/metadata addresses before issuing the request.","code_snippet":"1. **Act as the caller, stay RLS-constrained** — when a function wraps business logic but must still respect row ownership (e.g. an HTTP Function that a logged-in user calls to run a multi-step update). The caller's access token must reach the function and then be forwarded to the PG REST call:\n\n   ```js\n   const res = await fetch(`https://${envId}.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/rdb/rest/orders?select=*`, {\n     headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${callerAccessToken}` },\n   });\n   ```","intent":null,"tags":["Server-Side Request Forgery","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"bd886cfffc4a7513f8a5b80aac770a0ea9d905dc9520ad94055db95567528052","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":128,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SSRF3","finding_id":"finding-e69252c5075a4ebaabb2fd40a05d5e9b","category":"Server-Side Request Forgery","pattern":"Dynamic Request Target","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":139,"end_line":null},"finding":"fetch(`https://${","explanation":"Request target host is built from a dynamic or untrusted value. If the host is attacker-influenced, this enables SSRF to arbitrary internal or metadata endpoints.","remediation":"Do not build request URLs from untrusted input. Validate the host against an allowlist and reject internal/metadata addresses before issuing the request.","code_snippet":"1. **Act as the caller, stay RLS-constrained** — when a function wraps business logic but must still respect row ownership (e.g. an HTTP Function that a logged-in user calls to run a multi-step update). The caller's access token must reach the function and then be forwarded to the PG REST call:\n\n   ```js\n   const res = await fetch(`https://${envId}.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/rdb/rest/orders?select=*`, {\n     headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${callerAccessToken}` },\n   });\n   ```","intent":null,"tags":["Server-Side Request Forgery","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"bd886cfffc4a7513f8a5b80aac770a0ea9d905dc9520ad94055db95567528052","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/auth-and-rls.md","start_line":139,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-dd3965f5c19a480abd8314d84a16b8c4","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/http-api.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl \"https://<envId>.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/rdb/rest/todos?select=*&is_completed=eq.false\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <access_token>\"\n```\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"https://<envId>.api.tcloudbas","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"## Query examples\n\n```bash\ncurl \"https://<envId>.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/rdb/rest/todos?select=*&is_completed=eq.false\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <access_token>\"\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b3467d7b60e578cbf1e1a4dc9bfcc44704743dec6e74d7a8d83880e82c3e212a","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/http-api.md","start_line":32,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-2bc8bbbd144f4c10b4a43ebd7de79dbc","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/storage-pg.md","start_line":217,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST \"https://{envId}.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/storages/bucket/\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer {service_role_token}\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"### Via HTTP API (service_role only)\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"https://{envId}.api.tcloudbasegateway.com/v1/storages/bucket/\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer {service_role_token}\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\": \"avatars\", \"public\": false, \"file_size_limit\": 5242880, \"allowed_mime_types\": [\"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\"]}'","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"cfca87577518ead232481434b4b236940900b8c2c133ac4a2a62c185e0f86a3c","occurrences":[{"file":"references/postgresql-development-cloudbase/references/storage-pg.md","start_line":217,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-72c3f288eecb42eea8d23dda3cc4ff39","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/ops-inspector/references/fault-playbooks.md","start_line":139,"end_line":null},"finding":"without checking","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"- Trying to create a MySQL instance through MCP. Provisioning has been retired from the tool surface: new environments use PostgreSQL, and instances are only created in the console.\n- Treating document database tasks as MySQL management tasks.\n- Skipping `_openid` and permissions review after creating new SQL tables.\n- Destroying MySQL without explicit confirmation or without checking whether the environment still needs the instance.\n- Using `getConnectionInfo` (or inferred host/password) to build a default TCP client for new apps. Prefer SDK / `runQuery` / `runStatement`; TCP credentials are an explicit migration exception only.\n\n## When to use this skill","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9341b6f34d6af9081a0d6673f4217b7307d273da9f43357efd9029e15c5da76c","occurrences":[{"file":"references/ops-inspector/references/fault-playbooks.md","start_line":139,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-72c3f288eecb42eea8d23dda3cc4ff39","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/relational-database-mcp-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":44,"end_line":null},"finding":"without checking","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"- Trying to create a MySQL instance through MCP. Provisioning has been retired from the tool surface: new environments use PostgreSQL, and instances are only created in the console.\n- Treating document database tasks as MySQL management tasks.\n- Skipping `_openid` and permissions review after creating new SQL tables.\n- Destroying MySQL without explicit confirmation or without checking whether the environment still needs the instance.\n- Using `getConnectionInfo` (or inferred host/password) to build a default TCP client for new apps. Prefer SDK / `runQuery` / `runStatement`; TCP credentials are an explicit migration exception only.\n\n## When to use this skill","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9341b6f34d6af9081a0d6673f4217b7307d273da9f43357efd9029e15c5da76c","occurrences":[{"file":"references/relational-database-mcp-cloudbase/SKILL.md","start_line":44,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-41ae96cecc8449929371f2cf1f066a12","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/tooling-fallback.md","start_line":18,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document instructs agents to run `npx mcporter list` without pinning a specific package version or verifying package integrity. Because `npx` can fetch and execute the latest published package, a compromised upstream package, typo-squatted dependency, or malicious new release could result in arbitrary code execution on the operator's machine.","remediation":"Pin the exact package and version in the command (for example, use a fully qualified package name and version), and prefer an installed, audited dependency or lockfile-managed invocation over ad hoc `npx` execution. Add guidance to verify package provenance and avoid executing remote tooling implicitly during probing.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"references/tooling-fallback.md","start_line":18,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-97643e170ee14acf8b36f9137d1b8c6f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/ui-design/SKILL.md","start_line":173,"end_line":183},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly instructs the agent to use shell commands such as curl, wget, and Invoke-WebRequest to fetch remote assets into the project. That creates a command-and-network execution path where untrusted URLs or filenames from user input could lead to unsafe downloads, SSRF-like access attempts, or writing attacker-controlled files into the workspace; the warning to avoid private hosts helps but does not eliminate the risk.","remediation":"Remove direct shell-based download instructions from the skill, or replace them with a tightly constrained download mechanism that validates scheme, host allowlists, destination paths, file types, and size limits. If remote assets must be supported, require explicit user confirmation for each external URL, forbid interpolation of raw user input into shell commands, and document safe handling rules for filenames and storage locations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/ui-design/SKILL.md","start_line":173,"end_line":183}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b87d1ab2aa834db7b3dbc1985d5a384c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/web-development/frameworks.md","start_line":45,"end_line":46},"finding":null,"explanation":"The sample instructs storing an access token in `document.cookie` from client-side JavaScript without security attributes or warning about the consequences. That makes the token accessible to JavaScript and potentially exposed through XSS, weak cookie scoping, accidental transmission, or misuse in server-side auth flows, especially since the same document later shows API routes consuming that cookie.","remediation":"Avoid storing bearer access tokens in JavaScript-set cookies. Prefer secure server-managed session cookies with `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, and `SameSite` attributes, or keep short-lived tokens in memory and use a proper backend session exchange flow. If a cookie must be used, set it server-side with restrictive attributes, document the risks, and include CSRF/XSS mitigations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/web-development/frameworks.md","start_line":45,"end_line":46}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-0af597c893004646aad901483c2b65b8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":312,"end_line":312},"finding":null,"explanation":"A broad prototype-related phrase can match many ordinary design or product ideation requests that have nothing to do with CloudBase. In this skill map, that increases accidental activation risk and may steer users into unnecessary platform-specific reads or actions, reducing safety and correctness.","remediation":"Constrain prototype triggers with explicit CloudBase context, such as pairing 'prototype' with CloudBase app types, auth, database, or deployment terms. Add exclusion logic for generic design-only requests unless the prompt also references CloudBase, TCB, 微信云开发, or related APIs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/activation-map.yaml","start_line":312,"end_line":312}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c733f284aa9c445e84d7f5a1ff176c22","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/ai-model-wechat/SKILL.md","start_line":211,"end_line":211},"finding":null,"explanation":"Line L211 contains a natural-language restriction on how the agent must refer to third-party services: it says to use neutral phrasing and to not name specific competitor brands. This imposes an organizational language policy on outputs, but the file does not present it as a user choice or justify it as a necessary locale/compliance constraint.","remediation":"Either remove the brand-naming restriction, or clearly justify it as an organizational policy and scope it appropriately. If the skill must avoid certain brand references, document the reason and allow user-directed exceptions where appropriate.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/ai-model-wechat/SKILL.md","start_line":211,"end_line":211}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-5b479d68e0e44ae4ab3b5ccebb287a2f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"references/auth-tool-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":125,"end_line":125},"finding":null,"explanation":"The text states that SMS login is only supported in the `ap-shanghai` region, which imposes a locale/region constraint in natural language. While this may be technically true, the document does not frame it as a documented region-specific limitation or offer user choice, so it reads like a policy-level locale restriction.","remediation":"Clarify that this is a technical platform limitation rather than a mandated policy, e.g. explicitly state that SMS login is region-limited by CloudBase infrastructure and provide alternatives for other regions if available.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/auth-tool-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":125,"end_line":125}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-9c6e47c797474864b47a95c29a7609d4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":363,"end_line":363},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example validates phone input only against a mainland China mobile number pattern (`/^1[3-9]\\d{9}$/`), which implicitly restricts usage to a specific locale. The guide does not state that the skill is China-only or offer alternatives for other regions, so this appears to enforce a locale-specific assumption without opt-in.","remediation":"Document that the example is intended only for mainland China phone numbers, or make the example locale-aware by supporting international formats (for example E.164) or allowing users to choose their region before validation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/auth-web-cloudbase/references/extended-guide.md","start_line":363,"end_line":363}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-70e85a977d654eae801f26432dfa8b22","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/SKILL.md","start_line":34,"end_line":34},"finding":null,"explanation":"Line L34 presents a policy/instruction entirely in Chinese within an otherwise primarily English skill description. This imposes a specific language on part of the guidance without stating that Chinese is optional or providing an English equivalent, which can violate language/locale choice expectations.","remediation":"Provide the instruction in the document's primary language as well, or explicitly state that bilingual content is optional and offer both language versions side by side.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/SKILL.md","start_line":34,"end_line":34}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-44937943371947808be39f6e2d65107f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":36},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents the skill guidance entirely in Chinese, including title, instructions, and table descriptions, with no indication that users may choose another language. The policy explicitly calls for flagging language or locale constraints when a specific language is forced without user opt-in.","remediation":"State the intended language scope explicitly and justify it, or add a note that users may request/use another language version. If this repository is intentionally Chinese-only, document that constraint clearly in the file or associated skill description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/README.md","start_line":1,"end_line":36}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-8c201af011c54509b3b1a059f025329d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/pg-instance-spec.md","start_line":1,"end_line":304},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains user-facing operational guidance solely in Chinese, including prescribed wording for how to answer users. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language locale violation unless the restriction is explicitly justified, which is not documented here.","remediation":"State that the recipe is available in Chinese by default but allow responses in the user's preferred language, or add an explicit justification that this skill is intended only for a Chinese-language/tencent-cloud-specific audience.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/pg-instance-spec.md","start_line":1,"end_line":304}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-41fdb79fa6984425adb15c6018fd03d3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-usage-and-recycle.md","start_line":1,"end_line":75},"finding":null,"explanation":"All user-facing instructional content in this file is presented only in Chinese, and there is no indication that the user can opt into this language or that the skill is intentionally restricted to a Chinese-speaking audience. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy concern.","remediation":"Provide a language choice, add multilingual documentation, or explicitly document that the skill is intended for a Chinese-language audience and why that locale restriction is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-api-operations/references/recipes/platform-usage-and-recycle.md","start_line":1,"end_line":75}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1ba4b740ed0348dbbfb9db6e65d93c50","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/cloud-functions/SKILL.md","start_line":140,"end_line":140},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file is subject to natural-language policy checks. Line L140 contains a Chinese-language instruction embedded in an otherwise English skill guide, which can impose a language/locale expectation without user opt-in or documented justification.","remediation":"Keep the skill in a single declared language, or provide the same guidance bilingually with an explicit note that language choice is optional. If the Chinese text is required for a region-specific audience, document that scope clearly in the skill description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloud-functions/SKILL.md","start_line":140,"end_line":140}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-88021332b2f54c079c311f6f4ea58093","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":295,"end_line":301},"finding":null,"explanation":"Lines L295-L301 state 'Always select Python 3.10 runtime' and explicitly prohibit Python 3.9 or earlier. Under the policy, forced language/locale constraints can be findings when they are imposed without user opt-in; while this is technical rather than human-language locale, it is still a prescriptive language-version constraint presented as unconditional guidance rather than scoped choice.","remediation":"Clarify that Python 3.10 is required only for this CloudBase Agent deployment context, and explicitly note acceptable alternatives where supported. If the constraint is platform-specific, document that justification inline so it is clearly a context-bound requirement rather than a universal mandate.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/agent-deployment.md","start_line":295,"end_line":301}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4193c6b5b3d94775ae8a954ffe925753","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/server.md","start_line":22,"end_line":36},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents starting an HTTP server on port 9000 and includes a build pattern that enables external serving, but it does not warn readers that the skill will expose an API endpoint reachable over the network. Because SQP-2 applies to markdown files when descriptions omit warnings about behavior affecting system integrity or privacy, a brief disclosure about network exposure would improve safety.","remediation":"Add a short warning near the deployment examples stating that these commands start an HTTP service, may expose agent functionality over the network, and should be bound to trusted interfaces or protected by authentication as appropriate.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/server.md","start_line":22,"end_line":36}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a9e358b7e55d42be9a5af12cc4c0db15","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/cloudbase-agent/py/references/server.md","start_line":78,"end_line":89},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown includes sample code that reads the Authorization header and derives a user identifier from a bearer token, but there is no accompanying warning that the example processes sensitive authentication material. For markdown-scoped SQP-2, documentation should disclose credential-handling behavior that can affect privacy or security.","remediation":"Add a note beside the middleware example explaining th